\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rally but traders wary of  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 744 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 2006\par 03:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Oct 30 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , led by the Japanese yen, were broadly firm against the dollar on Monday after soft U.S. economic growth numbers reinforced a view that U.S. interest rates would stay steady for a while.  \par \par \uc2 But wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb strength in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tempered some of the gains.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) had stepped into the market to buy U.S. dollars and sell Singapore dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said its had again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the baht -- which rose to a 7-year high -- although the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had started to stabilise after inflows slowed.  \par \par \uc2 "The move in some Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been aggressive in the past week, and generally there is no resistance to the direction of the move but the magnitude," said DBS Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Philip Wee. "Generally the big picture is still not changed -- everyone is still looking for a weaker dollar."  \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=> climbed to 36.66 to the U.S. dollar, its strongest level since July 1999, before pulling back slightly by late trade.  \par \par \uc2 A Bangkok trader said there was strong support for the dollar around 36.35, but the outlook still suggested further baht gains.  \par \par \uc2 "Sellers of dollars are still strong," he said. "They (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) may just come in to calm the market down."  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar was quoted at 1.5610/20 <SGD=> per dollar, up about a quarter of a percent, but pulling away from a nine-year peak hit in offshore trade on Friday at about 1.5580.  \par \par \uc2 A dealer said he suspected the MAS had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday in the 1.5605 to 1.5620 per dollar area.  \par \par \uc2 FED OUTLOOK  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. economy grew at an annualised rate of 1.6 percent in the third quarter, its weakest pace in more than three years, due to a slump in the housing market, data showed on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 This set a backdrop for fresh gains in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which hit multi-week highs last week on foreign investment inflows, gains in the Chinese yuan and weakness in the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The yen strengthened more than 1 percent from levels traded late on Friday to about 117.20 yen per dollar <JPY=>, while the South Korean won firmed to a one-month high at about 942.60 to the dollar <KRW=>.  \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> rose about a quarter of a percent to 33.19 per U.S. dollar, its highest in just over a week.  \par \par \uc2 The Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> strengthened to about 3.6380 per dollar, its highest in more than three months, while the Philippine peso <PHP=> gained about a fifth of a percent to 49.73 to the U.S. dollar, its highest level in more than four years.  \par \par \uc2 "Dollar/yen weighed on dollar/peso at the open, but we are also seeing demand for pesos and some corporates are coming into the market," said a trader in Manila.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could come in at the 49.70 area." \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0745 GMT   \par \par