\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Steady, central banks in focus  \b0\par\par\uc2 814 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2006\par 04:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Oct 5 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were largely steady on Thursday, supported by a rally in the yen, but mostly sticking to familiar ranges and waiting for fresh direction.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the market was reluctant to take on big positions before Friday's key U.S. jobs report, while holidays in China and South Korea added to subdued trading activity.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=> was steady at about 37.60 per dollar, shrugging off comments from Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the baht rose too quickly.  \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> held steady at about 9,200 per dollar after Bank Indonesia delivered its fifth interest rate cut of the year, as expected.  \par \par \uc2 The key rate was lowered by half a percentage point to 10.75 percent and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said there was room for further cuts.  \par \par \uc2 "The decision was priced into the market and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to keep cutting rates to 9.75-10 percent by year end," said a Jakarta trader.  \par \par \uc2 "Bonds continue to rally but it's not that significant for the rupiah -- the correlation between the two is not that strong anymore and most buyers of debt are local players."  \par \par \uc2 The yen rose about 0.4 percent to around 117.55 yen per dollar <JPY=> and bounced back from Wednesday's one-month lows versus the euro <EURJPY=R>.  \par \par \uc2 DBS Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Philip Wee said the yen was due for a relief rally, which could spill over into Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "This has to do with falling oil prices and also an improving outlook for Japan's economy," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Oil prices have fallen sharply this week and held below $60 a barrel <CLc1> on Thursday. A pull-back in oil prices from record highs set in July is seen as positive for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as much of the region imports the bulk of its oil needs.  \par \par \uc2 YEN IMPACT  \par \par \uc2 Wee said the Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> and Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> were two Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that could benefit the most from a further recovery in the yen.  \par \par \uc2 The yen has been hurt in recent weeks as investors dump the low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for higher-yielding ones.  \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar firmed to 33.08 per U.S. dollar, off this week's nine-month lows at about 33.17, while the ringgit firmed about 0.1 percent to 3.6850 to the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 A comment by Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Zeti Akhtar Aziz on Thursday that a stronger ringgit will reinforce monetary policy helped support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But she added that the authorities had other policy instruments to deal with inflation.  \par \par \uc2 The prospect of rate cuts meanwhile was in focus in the Philippines after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it will discuss the possibility of such a move at its next policy meeting in November.  \par \par \uc2 Philippine consumer prices in September rose 5.7 percent from a year ago, slowing from a 6.3 percent increase in August.  \par \par \uc2 Some traders said they suspected the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on Thursday to keep the peso on the weak side of 50 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "It seems like 50 is the line in the sand for now and peso upside could slow for the time being," said Dresdner Kleinwort Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Sabrina Jacobs.  \par \par \uc2 The peso has risen about 7 percent since late June, hitting its highest level in more than four years earlier this week.  \par \par \uc2 "The prospect of a rate cut could put some pressure on the peso short-term," said a Manila trader. "But it depends on the magnitude of the move and the medium-term outlook is still positive." \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0816 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       117.72         118.06       +0.29\par  Sing dlr        1.5842         1.5859       +0.11\par  Taiwan dlr      33.088         33.120       +0.10\par  Baht             37.59          37.58       -0.03\par  Peso             49.93          50.01       +0.16\par  Rupiah         9202.00        9215.00       +0.14\par  Rupee            45.70          45.75       +0.10\par  Ringgit         3.6830         3.6890       +0.16\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       117.72         117.96       +0.20\par  Sing dlr        1.5842         1.6625       +4.94\par  Taiwan dlr      33.088         32.850       -0.72\par  Baht             37.59          41.11       +9.36\par  Peso             49.93          53.09       +6.33\par  Rupiah         9202.00        9835.00       +6.88\par  Rupee            45.70          45.04       -1.44\par  Ringgit         3.6830         3.7790       +2.61\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|