\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Ctrl Bk Dep Chief: Interest Rates Not Falling Yet  \b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2006\par 06:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Bank of Thailand Deputy Governor Tarisa Watanagase said Tuesday that declining inflation isn't enough for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to start cutting interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 "Inflation started to fall for only three months, that's not long enough to make us lower the interest rate. The interest rate is not on the downtrend yet," Tarisa told reporters. [ 03-10-06 0455GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Committee kept its key interest rate at 5.00% at its last two meetings after raising the rate steadily since August 2004 to curb inflation.  \par \par \uc2 Tarisa said the current decline in inflation was in line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's expectations.  \par \par \uc2 "The inflation risk has fallen substantially, but we have to wait and see more," she said.  \par \par \uc2 The Ministry of Commerce said Monday that headline inflation fell again in September to a 19-month low, due mainly to lower oil prices.  \par \par \uc2 The consumer price index rose 2.7% on year in September, compared with 3.8% in August. The CPI was down 0.3% from the previous month, after rising 0.1% on month in August. The month-on-month decline was the first since November last year.  \par \par \uc2 Tarisa said headline inflation for the whole year is expected to be below 5.0%. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier forecast the 2006 headline inflation at 5.0%-5.8%.  \par \par \uc2 Separately, Nitaya Pibulratanagit, assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, told reporters that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "The baht strengthened slightly early in line with the dollar weakness," Nitaya said.  \par \par \uc2 Asked whether the baht strength was due party to Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula's agreement to join the Cabinet team, Nitaya said she wasn't sure about that.  \par \par \uc2 At 0505 GMT, the dollar was quoted at THB37.565, down from THB37.59 early and from THB37.615 at Monday's close in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 -By Bangkok Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Mary de Wet [ 03-10-06 0531GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020061003e2a30003w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
