\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Thai Ctrl Bk Rate Unchanged; "Too Early" For Cut  \b0\par\par\uc2 1,051 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2006\par 12:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    (Updates with analyst comments, more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  comments) \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Bank of Thailand left its benchmark 14-day target rate unchanged at 5.0% Wednesday, saying that despite a slowdown in the country's economic growth rate, it is too early to consider any reduction in interest rates.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 The steady policy decision was in line with expectations and underlines a shift by many central banks in Asia to focus on growth rather than inflation in setting policy.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement that the economy is adjusting well as a slight slowdown in growth has been partially offset by a favorable export performance.  \par \par \uc2 "It's too early to talk about a declining interest rate trend now, because inflation has only been declining for a few months," Assistant Governor Atchana Waiquamdee said at a press conference.  \par \par \uc2 Oil prices have fallen somewhat, but the risk of future volatility and accompanying inflation remain, "so the current level of the policy rate was considered appropriate," the statement said.  \par \par \uc2 The baht and the country's stock and bond markets were unmoved, as the rate decision and the maintenance of a neutral policy stance were signaled by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments on recent data, which have showed a softening in both economic growth and inflation.  \par \par \uc2 Standard Chartered Bank senior economist Usara Wilaipich said domestic demand remains weak as consumption and investment decisions continue to be postponed due to political uncertainty, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's neutral stance is the correct one.  \par \par \uc2 "There is no need to rush. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still has time to wait for more evidence that inflation is on a (sustained) decline," Usara said.  \par \par \uc2 Economists polled recently by Dow Jones Newswires forecast on average that Bank of Thailand will start cutting its 14-day repurchase market target rate from the current level of 5.0% in the second quarter of 2007.  \par \par \uc2 "The next move in interest rates should be a cut in 2007, once inflation has clearly headed south, and we are sure the Fed is done," Usara said.  \par \par \uc2 Usara said she believes that the U.S. Federal Reserve has completed its tightening cycle, but there is a risk that U.S. fed funds rate could rise one more time from its current level of 5.25%.  \par \par \uc2 Atchana said it isn't necessary for Thailand to follow U.S. rates, but the tightening cycles have been correlated because local inflation in both countries was driven by global oil prices. An interest rate differential of 25-to-50 basis points between the two countries is too small to have a significant effect on capital flows, she said.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets recently to prevent the baht from outperforming other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar, in order to maintain the competitiveness of the country's vital export sector.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed in Asian trade Wednesday at THB37.35, just above the six-year low of THB37.28 it set on Aug. 11.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Inflation-Adjusted Rates Back In Positive Territory \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Currently, however, other factors are playing a bigger role than exchange-rate management in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision-making process on interest rates.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Atchana said second-quarter gross domestic product growth at 4.9% on year and a seasonally-adjusted 1.0% on quarter was slightly better than the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  expected, so growth isn't an overriding concern at the moment. In the first quarter, GDP was up 6.1% on year and 0.8% on quarter.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If core inflation falls further, there will be more room for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to focus on economic growth," Atchana said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Core inflation eased to 1.9% on year in August from a peak of 2.9% in April. The monetary policy committee has an official core inflation-targeting range of zero to 3.5%.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's headline inflation rate has fallen to 3.9% on year in August from a peak of 6.2% in May, due mainly to a rising base of comparison resulting from the elimination of a diesel price subsidy in July 2005.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Atchana said oil prices have declined recently, but they could start to climb again if - for example - there is a terrorist attack. Therefore, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can't assume that the downward trend in oil prices will continue, and the risk of higher inflation remains.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is leaving its estimate of the average Dubai oil price this year at $71 a barrel, she said. Thailand traditionally uses Dubai oil prices as its benchmark.Early Wednesday, cash Dubai was assessed by Dow Jones Newswires at $64.72-$64.77.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, analysts said a quick move to cut interest rates wouldn't remove political uncertainty, which is one of the major factors holding back growth in investment and consumption.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand has been under a caretaker government since parliament was dissolved in February. The results of elections held in April were annulled due to irregularities, and fresh polls scheduled for Oct. 15 may be delayed because a new Election Commission is still in the process of selection.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Formation of a new government - likely late this year or early next year - is expected to release pent-up investment demand in the second and third quarter of next year, so a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate cut would have a more positive effect on growth at that time.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand's long-held desire to encourage savings by pushing commercial bank deposit account interest rates above the rate of inflation was another factor supporting the decision to leave the policy rate unchanged.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Atchana said the country's real interest rate - based on an average deposit rate adjusted for expected inflation - has finally returned to positive territory at 0.12%, from minus 0.4% at the time of the previous monetary policy committee meeting on July 19.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Returning real deposit rates to positive territory was one of the reasons cited by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for an aggressive tightening cycle in which the 14-day target rate rose 375 basis points in 13 steps over 15 meetings between August 2004 and June 2006.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Suttinee Yuvejwattana and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Iain McDonald [ 06-09-06 1003GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060906e296000oi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
