\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends Up, Off High On Ctrl Bk Action; Bonds Jump  \b0\par\par\uc2 666 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2006\par 12:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended marginally stronger against the U.S. dollar Tuesday, off an early high after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to help curb the baht's strength, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices ended sharply higher as the yield curve flattened again ahead of Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monetary Policy Committee meeting. Recent trends in economic data and related comments from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  make it almost certain that the MPC will retain a neutral policy stance and leave its 14-day repurchase market target rate unchanged at 5%.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at THB37.34, versus THB37.36 at the Asian close Monday, after moving in a tight range between THB37.33 and THB37.38.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the dollar opened around the day's low. Offshore players continued to unload the U.S. unit, as the dollar was weak against most key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 However, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  agents were buying dollars late Monday and also Tuesday, helping to slow the baht's rise toward the six-year high it set last month at THB37.28 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "Offshore banks, which were suspected to be \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  agents, stepped in to buy the dollar around the THB37.33-THB37.35 level during the day, helping to cap the dollar's downside. Without the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action, the dollar would have fallen further," said a local bank trader.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Assistant Governor Nitaya Pibulratanagit said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday, but the amount wasn't much.  \par \par \uc2 Nitaya said the baht's strength was in line with the global weakness of the dollar, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed to take action in a bid to reduce the effect on exporters.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said THB37.30 was likely to remain a key support for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday due to expectations the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to defend that level. Stiff resistance is tipped around THB37.45 for any dollar rebound. [ 05-09-06 1006GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Thai government bond yields fell sharply again as foreign funds optimistic about prospects for the baht added to demand from big local funds that already outstripped local supply, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Thailand sold at auction Tuesday THB15 billion of its 364-day bonds at an average accepted yield of 5.07786%, down from 5.17086% at last week's auction.  \par \par \uc2 Long-term yields have dropped about 20 basis points and medium-term yields about 10 basis points in the first two days of the week, already matching last week's flattening.  \par \par \uc2 The average bid on the government bond due August 2008 fell four basis points to 5.078%, the July 2016 bid was down seven basis points to 5.167%, and the July 2026 bid plunged 15 basis points to end at 5.317%, according to the Web site of the Thai Bond Market Association.  \par \par \uc2 An upward correction isn't expected because inflation is on a downward trend, but there is little further room for flattening because the Bank of Thailand is almost certain to leave its 14-day repurchase market target rate unchanged at 5% when it meets Wednesday, and cuts in the policy rate aren't expected until around the second quarter of 2007.  \par \par \uc2 The most-active overnight interbank interest rate was expected to have remained around 4.95%.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market      Term            Tuesday               Monday \par Interbank   Overnight/ \par             Most-Active     4.95000% (Estimate)   4.95000% \par Repurchase  Overnight/Close 4.90625%              4.87500% \par             14-Day/Close    5.00000%              5.00000% \par Bibor       3-Month/11 am   5.38938%              5.39750% \par             6-Month/11 am   5.45063%              5.46344% \par THB Fix     6-Month/11 am   5.46704%              5.47123% \par THB IRS Fix 2-Year/11 am    5.45%                 5.44% \par             10-Year/11 am   5.74%                 5.74% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Suttinee Yuvejwattana and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2266 0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Graham Norris [ 05-09-06 1016GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1028 1861  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060905e295000ka\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
