\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Thai Baht Ends Up, Off High On Ctrl Bk Action  \b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2006\par 12:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2006, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended marginally stronger against the U.S. dollar Tuesday, off an early high after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to help curb the baht's strength, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices ended sharply higher as the yield curve flattened again ahead of Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monetary Policy Committee meeting. Recent trends in economic data and related comments from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  make it almost certain that the MPC will retain a neutral policy stance and leave its 14-day repurchase market target rate unchanged at 5%.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at THB37.34, versus THB37.36 at the Asian close Monday, after moving in a tight range between THB37.33 and THB37.38.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the dollar opened around the day's low. Offshore players continued to unload the U.S. unit, as the dollar was weak against most key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 However, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  agents were buying dollars late Monday and also Tuesday, helping to slow the baht's rise toward the six-year high it set last month at THB37.28 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 'Offshore banks, which were suspected to be \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  agents, stepped in to buy the dollar around the THB37.33-THB37.35 level during the day, helping to cap the dollar's downside. Without the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action, the dollar would have fallen further,' said a local bank trader.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Assistant Governor Nitaya Pibulratanagit said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday, but the amount wasn't much.  \par \par \uc2 Nitaya said the baht's strength was in line with the global weakness of the dollar, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed to take action in a bid to reduce the effect on exporters.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said THB37.30 was likely to remain a key support for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday due to expectations the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to defend that level. Stiff resistance is tipped around THB37.45 for any dollar rebound.  \par \par \uc2 -0-   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020060905e2950050l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
