\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends Tad Up On Exporters Dlr Selling; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 655 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2006\par 12:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended marginally stronger against the U.S. dollar in Asian spot trade Friday, with exporters' dollar selling taking it off an early low, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices rose on continued buying by customers of commercial banks - funds and corporations.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at THB37.66, down from THB37.685 at the Asian close Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened at the day's high of THB37.73, led by offshore dollar buying in line with its broad strength overnight.  \par \par \uc2 However, it failed to sustain its gains as exporters jumped in to unload the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A number of local players also took profit on the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Trading volume was moderate. Traders said most players remained on the sidelines, waiting for fresh leads and a clearer view of the Thai political situation.  \par \par \uc2 "There has been lots of news and rumors. They didn't spark buying or selling, but most investors prefer to wait and see until they know what's going on," said a local bank trader.  \par \par \uc2 A bomb was found in a car that was driven back and forth outside caretaker Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra's home Thursday, and an army lieutenant was charged with illegal possession of an explosive device. The junior officer was once a driver for army General Pallop Pinmanee, who was sacked.  \par \par \uc2 However, Pallop said Friday that the alleged assassination attempt was fabricated by the prime minister himself. Local newspapers also reported speculation that the alleged plot was an attempt by the government to divert attention from other issues ahead of general elections scheduled for Oct. 15.  \par \par \uc2 Traders expect the dollar to trade over the weekend in a range of THB37.60-THB37.75.  \par \par \uc2 Looking ahead, the dollar's downside is expected to be supported firmly at THB37.50 due to likely \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said late Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will do its best to slow the baht's rise and reduce the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's volatility. [ 25-08-06 1048GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The Thai government bond yield curve flattened on strong demand in the long end from banks' customers - local funds and corporations - which have forced banks into the market to refill trading portfolios despite some concerns about how far yields can fall, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Many analysts don't expect interest rates to begin to decline until around the second quarter of next year, but the prospect of lower rates helps to make long bonds a relatively safe place to park cash while waiting for a new government to be formed late this year or early next year.  \par \par \uc2 In the secondary market, the average bid on the government bond due November 2009 was down two basis points at 5.257%, the July 2016 bid fell three basis points to 5.395%, and the July 2026 bid dropped five basis points to end at 5.683%, according to the Web site of the Thai Bond Market Association.  \par \par \uc2 Interest rate swaps were also three to six basis points lower, reflecting the decline in yields and expectations that inflation will continue to slow significantly in the second half of the year.  \par \par \uc2 The most-active overnight interbank interest rate was expected to have remained around 4.95%.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market      Term            Friday                Thursday \par Interbank   Overnight/ \par             Most-Active     4.95000% (Estimate)   4.95000% \par Repurchase  Overnight/Close 4.84375%              4.84375% \par             14-Day/Close    5.00000%              5.00000% \par Bibor       3-Month/11 am   5.40156%              5.40156% \par             6-Month/11 am   5.49500%              5.49500% \par THB Fix     6-Month/11 am   5.52404%              5.52954% \par THB IRS Fix 2-Year/11 am    5.59%                 5.62% \par             10-Year/11 am   5.87%                 5.93% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Suttinee Yuvejwattana and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2266 0744; tom.fox@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Hilary Mc Cully and Michael Kitchen [ 25-08-06 1051GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1028 1861  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060825e28p000k1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
