\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Thai Baht Ends Tad Up On Exporters Dlr Selling; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2006\par 13:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2006, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended marginally stronger against the U.S. dollar in Asian spot trade Friday, with exporters' dollar selling taking it off an early low, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices rose on continued buying by customers of commercial banks - funds and corporations.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at THB37.66, down from THB37.685 at the Asian close Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened at the day's high of THB37.73, led by offshore dollar buying in line with its broad strength overnight.  \par \par \uc2 However, it failed to sustain its gains as exporters jumped in to unload the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A number of local players also took profit on the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Trading volume was moderate. Traders said most players remained on the sidelines, waiting for fresh leads and a clearer view of the Thai political situation.  \par \par \uc2 'There has been lots of news and rumors. They didn't spark buying or selling, but most investors prefer to wait and see until they know what's going on,' said a local bank trader.  \par \par \uc2 A bomb was found in a car that was driven back and forth outside caretaker Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra's home Thursday, and an army lieutenant was charged with illegal possession of an explosive device. The junior officer was once a driver for army General Pallop Pinmanee, who was sacked.  \par \par \uc2 However, Pallop said Friday that the alleged assassination attempt was fabricated by the prime minister himself. Local newspapers also reported speculation that the alleged plot was an attempt by the government to divert attention from other issues ahead of general elections scheduled for Oct. 15.  \par \par \uc2 Traders expect the dollar to trade over the weekend in a range of THB37.60-THB37.75.  \par \par \uc2 Looking ahead, the dollar's downside is expected to be supported firmly at THB37.50 due to likely \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said late Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will do its best to slow the baht's rise and reduce the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's volatility.  \par \par \uc2 -0-   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020060825e28p005po\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
