\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Thai Ctrl Bker:Econ Recovers, Baht Volatile In 07  \b0\par\par\uc2 855 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 2006\par 18:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (This updates an item published at 1503 GMT with more comment from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor.)  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Thailand's business sectors will face global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market volatility until the end of next year, but growth in the local economy could recover before then, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said.  \par \par \uc2 In a dinner speech late Thursday, Pridiyathorn said global capital flows in an out of Asia have kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  busy several times this year already, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets sometimes almost 24 hours a day to reduce volatility in the baht.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will maintain its role of reducing baht volatility as much as it can, but exporters and other business sectors have to prepare themselves (for baht strength) because the dollar trend is weak," due to the massive U.S. current account deficit, he said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed Thursday in Asia at THB37.685, up from a six-and-a-half-year low of THB37.28 Aug. 11, with help from heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week.  \par \par \uc2 Pridiyathorn said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't work miracles to pin the baht down at one place, however, and it won't act against the trend.  \par \par \uc2 Thai businesses can expect \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility from swings in global capital flows to continue until the end of next year, he said. He didn't elaborate, but was apparently referring to adjustments global investors have been making in preparation for an imminent peak and a reversal likely next year in the U.S. interest rate cycle.  \par \par \uc2 While external volatility will remain a risk, however, local economic fundamentals are relatively stable, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Gross domestic product growth will likely slow to a range of 3%-4% on year in the second half of the year from an estimated 5.4% on year in the first half, for full-year 2006 growth of around 4.5%, he said.  \par \par \uc2 But GDP growth next year is likely to exceed 4.5% as pent-up investment surges after the formation of a new government, Pridiyathorn said.  \par \par \uc2 His figures were in line with the latest official \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  forecasts. Growth next year is projected in a range of 4%-5.25%.  \par \par \uc2 Growth has been slowing due to high oil prices and interest rates, and to slumping confidence in an extended period of political uncertainty.  \par \par \uc2 Thailand has been without a working legislature under a caretaker government since parliament was dissolved in February. The results of snap polls held April 2 were annulled due to irregularities. General elections scheduled Oct. 15 may be delayed while an Election Commission is chosen, but a new government is expected to be formed by late this year or early next year.  \par \par \uc2 Pridiyathorn said private investment will have to rise after political uncertainty eases, because capacity utilization has risen to 76%, where it stood before the Asian financial crisis of 1997.  \par \par \uc2 In the meantime, growth in investment and consumption will slow further, and exports will likely begin to slow if global demand eases as expected.  \par \par \uc2 But public spending is emerging to support the economy through the rough patch in the second half of this year, Pridiyathorn said.  \par \par \uc2 Due in part to the political uncertainty, public spending was down 0.3% on year in the first half, but the caretaker government has moved to accelerate spending under the current budget in the current third quarter of the calendar year, which is the final quarter of the fiscal year 2006, he said.  \par \par \uc2 In the coming quarter ending Dec. 31, 2006, the first quarter of fiscal 2007, the caretaker government plans to speed up carryover spending, and public spending is expected to rise 11% on year in the second half of the calendar year, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Later, Governor Pridiyathorn told reporters government spending can't be counted on as driver of growth next year. An expanded budget for the fiscal year beginning Oct. 1, 2006 probably won't be approved by a new parliament until the first or second quarter of the next calendar year.  \par \par \uc2 Exports have been the main engine of growth in 2006 and will continue to be the main driver next year, so the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't let the baht strengthen too much, Pridiyathorn said.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Thailand does incur costs from issuing baht-denominated bonds to sterilize the effects on the local money supply of buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the baht's rise. However, the income from investing the increased foreign reserves is close to the interest cost of the bonds, there isn't much effect on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves stood at $59.4 billion as of Aug. 11.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, despite expectations both local and U.S. interest rates are at or near a peak and could begin falling next year, Pridiyathorn said he couldn't comment on the long-term outlook for Thai interest rates, because global oil prices continue fluctuating.  \par \par \uc2 -By Suttinee Yuvejwattana and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2266 0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com [ 24-08-06 1620GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060824e28o000tj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
