own 0.3% on year in the first half, but the caretaker government has moved to accelerate spending under the current budget in the current third quarter of the calendar year, which is the final quarter of the fiscal year 2006, he said.  \par \par \uc2 In the coming quarter ending Dec. 31, 2006, the first quarter of fiscal 2007, the caretaker government plans to speed up carryover spending, and public spending is expected to rise 11% on year in the second half of the calendar year, he said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Suttinee Yuvejwattana and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2266 0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com [ 24-08-06 1503GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060824e28o000qt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
