\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Fin Min:Baht Should Rise No More Than 3-3.5% Per Yr  \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2006\par 05:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht should appreciate at no more than 3.0%-3.5% each year, a rate that will allow businesses to adapt comfortably to exchange-rate movements, Finance Minister Thanong Bidaya said Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Thanong told reporters that the appropriate dollar level for this year is between THB37.50 and THB38.00, while that for next year is around THB37.50. [ 23-08-06 0406GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the baht's strength is a short-term measure to prevent excessive inflows that might lead to a rapid rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value, which would hurt the economy and exports, Thanong said.  \par \par \uc2 "The movement of the baht should be gradual. If it needs to be firmer, it should rise in steps," said Thanong.  \par \par \uc2 At 0410 GMT Wednesday, the dollar was at THB37.605, barely changed from THB37.61 early. It has weakened from THB41.025 at the beginning of this year.  \par \par \uc2 Thanong said the baht's firmer tone is in line with a regional trend doesn't substantially affect the country's competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 Still, he expressed concerns over a possible slowdown in investment, which could weigh on economic growth.  \par \par \uc2 Many business operators have deferred their investments due to domestic political uncertainty and higher interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 "I personally expect economic growth this year to be between 4.2% and 4.5%, and next year between 3.75% and 4.0%," Thanong said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official growth forecast for this calendar year ranges from 4.0%-5.0%. The ministry hasn't yet issued its growth projection for next year.  \par \par \uc2 -By Bangkok Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Ven Ram [ 23-08-06 0455GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060823e28n0003i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
