\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends Down On Foreign Bks' Dlr Buying; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 690 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2006\par 13:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended softer against the dollar Thursday on substantial buying of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by two major foreign banks, despite a generally bearish dollar tone, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices rose in line with overnight gains in U.S. Treasurys after an issue of data that indicated U.S. inflationary pressures are easing.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at THB37.585, up from THB37.43 at the Asian close Wednesday, after moving in an intraday range of THB37.44 to THB37.62.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the heavy dollar buying may simply have been profit-taking, or it could be linked to speculation that the acquisition of a controlling stake in Thai telecommunications conglomerate Shin Corp. PCL (SHIN.TH) by Singapore's Temasek Holding (TEMAH.YY) may be reversed if the commerce ministry rules that a local holding company involved in the deal is serving as a nominee for Temasek.  \par \par \uc2 The big dollar buying orders came from a U.S. bank and a Swiss-based bank, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "It's not common to see any parties buying such a huge amount, especially while the overall dollar trend is softening... However, they didn't seem to be acting on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the authorities don't normally move this aggressively," one local trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Profit-taking would be a plausible explanation, as funds may have decided to sell off positions after failing to take the baht past resistance from Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a 6.5-year high at THB37.28 against the dollar Friday.  \par \par \uc2 But renewed concerns about the Shin-Temasek deal may have contributed to the dollar buying.  \par \par \uc2 An initial investigation by the Commerce Ministry found evidence that the local Kularb Kaew Ltd. could be a nominee for Temasek, which would mean that the Singapore government investment arm owns a stake in Shin in excess of the limit on foreign ownership, Deputy Permanent Secretary for Commerce Yanyong Phuangrach told reporters Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 He said further information is needed before the ministry can reach a conclusion, however. The ministry will take around two months to finalize the matter and forward its findings to the police, who will consider whether to refer the case to court, Yanyong said.  \par \par \uc2 The findings aren't likely to have a long-term effect on the baht, however, because Yanyong said any confirmation that Kularb Kaew is a nominee for Temasek would only require that share holdings be adjusted, and any legal charges would be brought against the local holding company.  \par \par \uc2 Dollar selling by exporters around THB37.60 limited the U.S. unit's gains, providing immediate resistance.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar to find next firm resistance at THB37.80 while support is pegged at THB37.40. [ 17-08-06 1108GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Thai government bond yields ended lower, tracking the reaction of U.S. Treasury yields to data issued overnight indicating U.S. inflation pressures are easing, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The average bid on the government bond due November 2009 eased almost 1/2 basis point to 5.296%, the July 2016 bid fell three basis points to 5.483% and the July 2026 bid was down one basis point to end at 5.789, according to the Web site of the Thai Bond Market Association.  \par \par \uc2 Yields were expected to remain range bound with limited room to decline due to stable money market interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 The most-active overnight interbank interest rate was expected to have remained around 4.95%.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market      Term            Thursday              Wednesday \par Interbank   Overnight/ \par             Most-Active     4.95000% (Estimate)   4.95000% \par Repurchase  Overnight/Close 4.84375%              4.84375% \par             14-Day/Close    5.00000%              5.00000% \par Bibor       3-Month/11 am   5.40156%              5.40208% \par             6-Month/11 am   5.49875%              5.49958% \par THB Fix     6-Month/11 am   5.51829%              5.55586% \par THB IRS Fix 2-Year/11 am    5.62%                 5.65% \par             10-Year/11 am   5.91%                 5.92% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Phisanu Phromchanya and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2266 0744; djnews.bangkokdowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Hilary Mc Cully [ 17-08-06 1111GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1028 1861  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060817e28h000h7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
