\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Thai baht restrained by  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 805 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2006\par 04:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 16 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose on Wednesday, some of them after several days of losses against the dollar, following soft U.S. producer price data that reduced expectations of further rate rises by the Federal Reserve.  \par \par \uc2 Extended declines in crude oil prices also inspired gains.  \par \par \uc2 The yen <JPY=> rallied more than half a percent to around 116 per dollar. The Singapore dollar <SGD=> and Philippine peso <PHP=> regained the quarter percent they lost on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> was flat around 9,100 a dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The baht <THB=> was among Wednesday's biggest gainers although its rise was thwarted by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 It was quoted around 37.32/35 per dollar, staying on the weaker side of Friday's 6-1/2-year high of 37.215 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Traders offered various reasons for the baht's 1.8 percent climb in the past 2 weeks, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  attributed its rise to foreign inflows into Thai equity and bond markets.  \par \par \uc2 Some said Singapore state investment firm Temasek Holdings [TEM.UL] was repaying a baht loan taken earlier this year when it bought a stake in telecoms group Shin Corp . That loan was estimated to be about $1 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Another trader said the cash inflows into Thailand were to fund a likely sale of Bank of Ayudhya's 25 percent stake to General Electric .  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  confused traders, since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had said earlier this month it would allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate in line with market forces.  \par \par \uc2 "These are sort of lumpy flows which are not going to be sustainable," said Sriyan Pietersz, JPMorgan's chief Thai strategist.  \par \par \uc2 "While I do think we will see more foreign inflows on the equity side in the months to come, I don't think they are going to be that large," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts also said that by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rein in the baht, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was helping Temasek get a better rate for its loan repayment.  \par \par \uc2 "The BOT's motive is to stop dollar/baht doing down. But by default, they end up pushing dollar/baht higher so it makes it cheaper for Temasek to buy baht," one analyst said.  \par \par \uc2 TAIWAN FLOWS  \par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, Taiwan's stock market <.TW11> rose 1.23 percent on the back of a heavy $312 million foreign net portfolio inflow. Yet, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <TWD=TP> was rangebound around 32.75 per U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said more inflows into Asian markets were likely as the view that U.S. rates have peaked gets entrenched.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. core producer prices fell 0.3 percent in July from June, surprising analysts who had expected a rise. Consumer price inflation is due on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "Any signs that the Fed was correct to pause this month will be taken as a positive for risky assets," ABN AMRO strategist Shahab Jalinoos said in a note.  \par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under selling pressure earlier this week after robust U.S. retail sales data stoked expectations the Fed might renew a two-year tightening campaign after leaving rates unchanged last week.  \par \par \uc2 Crude oil, which the region imports in large quantities, fell below $73 a barrel after a U.N.-brokered truce ended fighting between Israel and Lebanon's Hizbollah.  \par \par \uc2 China's yuan <CNY=CFXS> also rose on Wednesday, recovering from the previous day's sharp fall to a three-week low.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0820 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       115.99         116.59       +0.52\par  Sing dlr        1.5770         1.5802       +0.20\par  Taiwan dlr      32.733         32.750       +0.05\par  Korean won      965.00         965.40       +0.04\par  Baht             37.36          37.44       +0.21\par  Peso             51.23          51.44       +0.41\par  Rupiah         9089.00        9094.00       +0.06\par  Rupee            46.57          46.62       +0.11\par  Ringgit         3.6800         3.6800       +0.00\par  Yuan            7.9902         7.9985       +0.10\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       115.99         117.96       +1.70\par  Sing dlr        1.5770         1.6625       +5.42\par  Taiwan dlr      32.733         32.850       +0.36\par  Korean won      965.00        1011.60       +4.83\par  Baht             37.36          41.11      +10.04\par  Peso             51.23          53.09       +3.63\par  Rupiah         9089.00        9835.00       +8.21\par  Rupee            46.57          45.04       -3.28\par  Ringgit         3.6800         3.7790       +2.69\par  Yuan            7.9902         8.0702       +1.00\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument