\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends Weaker On Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Dn  \b0\par\par\uc2 664 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 2006\par 12:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht retreated Tuesday after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed that it continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to curb the baht's strength after it hit a six-and-a-half year high Friday, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 However, the baht's fall was limited by offshore parties' dollar selling and the U.S. unit's generally soft tone against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in intraday trading, they said.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices ended lower, in line with movement in the U.S. Treasury market since late Friday following stronger-than-expected U.S. retail sales data.  \par \par \uc2 Thai financial markets were closed Monday for a public holiday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at THB37.46, up from THB37.36 at the Asian close Friday, after moving in a range of THB37.36-THB37.46.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar shot up on news that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had entered the market. However, the verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  couldn't spur a sharp rally as some offshore parties unloaded dollars in the afternoon," said a dealer at a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said Tuesday the baht was too strong and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had stepped in during the day to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.  \par \par \uc2 "The baht is slightly too strong. We will ensure that it weakens slightly, but we will not oppose the baht's market trend," Pridiyathorn said.  \par \par \uc2 The governor said there were hefty equity-related inflows Friday, which were partially responsible for the baht's strength.  \par \par \uc2 Traders expect the dollar's immediate resistance at THB37.50 to cap the upside in the short term while support is pegged around THB37.35, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to take action to limit the baht's rise.  \par \par \uc2 The baht has been outperforming regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far this year with a rise of about 11%. JPMorgan said in a report Monday, however, that although Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit the baht's gains, it is unlikely to try to reverse those gains because the strength of the baht helps weaken the passthrough to local inflation from higher global oil prices. [ 15-08-06 1045GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The Thai government bond yields rose slightly, playing catch up with increases in U.S. Treasury yields late Friday and Monday on signs of strength in the U.S. economy, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 However, strong demand in Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond auction helped take some of the yields off their early highs.  \par \par \uc2 Investors will be watching demand and yield levels in Wednesday's auction of 20-year bonds, as moderate local supply conditions will likely continue to mute the effects of recent increases in U.S. yields.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Thailand sold at auction Tuesday THB10 billion worth of its 364-day bonds at an average 5.18887%, down from 5.20967% at last week's auction in line with secondary market bid levels.  \par \par \uc2 The average bid on the government bond due November 2009 rose two basis points to 5.316%, the July 2016 bid was up three basis points to 5.507% and the July 2026 bid added two basis points to end at 5.794%, according to the Web site of the Thai Bond Market Association.  \par \par \uc2 The most-active overnight interbank interest rate was expected to have remained in its recent range of 4.94%-4.95%.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market      Term            Tuesday               Friday \par Interbank   Overnight/ \par             Most-Active     4.94%-4.95%(Estimate) 4.95000% \par Repurchase  Overnight/Close 4.84375%              4.84375% \par             14-Day/Close    5.00000%              5.00000% \par Bibor       3-Month/11 am   5.40234%              5.40313% \par             6-Month/11 am   5.50078%              5.50031% \par THB Fix     6-Month/11 am   5.58412%              5.53421% \par THB IRS Fix 2-Year/11 am    5.68%                 5.66% \par             10-Year/11 am   5.93%                 5.91% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Phisanu Phromchanya and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2266 0744; djnews.bangkokdowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Hilary Mc Cully [ 15-08-06 1046GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1028 1861  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060815e28f000fv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
