\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends Up, Hits 6.5-Yr High; Short-End Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 741 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2006\par 13:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht extended its rally to end just off a six-and-a-half year high Friday as a torrent of offshore selling continued to weaken the dollar despite suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Thai long-term government bonds were mostly unchanged, but prices of short-term treasury bills rose due to expectations that interest rates have peaked. The pressure from the short end caused prices of some medium-term bonds to rise as well.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at THB37.36, down from THB37.46 at the Asian close Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Offshore players continued to dump the dollar, which has been on a losing streak against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently due to expectations that U.S. interest rates may have peaked.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar slid to THB37.28 in the afternoon, its lowest level since January 2000. It reached an intraday high of THB37.44 in the morning.  \par \par \uc2 But the U.S. unit staged a good recovery in late trade due to buying that was likely a combination of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action and players' adjustments to the dollar's rebound against key Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the Japanese yen.  \par \par \uc2 Traders suspect Bank of Thailand once again bought dollars to help limit the baht's strength. Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula confirmed late Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been active in the market. Traders said the greenback could sink to THB37.15 in foreign markets over the long weekend with the local market closed Monday for a public holiday, unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps in during the holiday, support (for the dollar-baht exchange rate) would be around THB37.23-THB37.30," said a local trader. "If not, it could fall to THB37.15 by Tuesday morning."  \par \par \uc2 Thai Finance Minister Thanong Bidaya attempted to assist the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  with some mild verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday by saying the baht's strength during the past 2-3 days is likely a short term situation, and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the means to temper the effects of volatile capital flows.  \par \par \uc2 "There is no unusual movement in the market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also monitoring the market closely," Thanong told reporters. [ 11-08-06 1103GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The Thai government bond yield curve steepened slightly due to demand for short-term paper on a market view that local interest rates have peaked, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Medium-term yields eased slightly under the pull of short-term yields, but except for the very shortest terms, declines were limited to one basis point.  \par \par \uc2 Further declines in short- and medium-term yields might follow if demand is as strong as expected at Tuesday's auction of THB10 billion worth of 364-day \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds.  \par \par \uc2 The 364-day term was bid Friday at 5.19%, down from 5.20% Thursday, while the bid on 182-day paper eased to 4.98% from 4.99%.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier Friday, the Bank of Thailand sold THB6 billion worth of 28-day treasury bills at 4.78990%, down from an average of 4.84283% at Monday's auction. Another THB7 billion of 91-day t-bills was sold at an average 4.86644%, down from 4.90111%. But THB7 billion of 182-day t-bills was sold at an average 4.98429%, up marginally from 4.98053%.  \par \par \uc2 The average bid on the government bond due November 2009 fell one and 1/2 basis points to 5.298%, the July 2016 bid was almost flat at 5.474%, and the July 2026 bid was nearly unchanged at 5.771%, according to the Web site of the Thai Bond Market Association.  \par \par \uc2 The most-active overnight interbank interest rate was expected to have remained in its recent range of 4.94%-4.95%.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market      Term            Friday                Thursday \par Interbank   Overnight/ \par             Most-Active     4.94%-4.95%(Estimate) 4.94000% \par Repurchase  Overnight/Close 4.84375%              4.87500% \par             14-Day/Close    5.00000%              5.00000% \par Bibor       3-Month/11 am   5.40313%              5.40438% \par             6-Month/11 am   5.50031%              5.50156% \par THB Fix     6-Month/11 am   5.53421%              5.53366% \par THB IRS Fix 2-Year/11 am    5.66%                 5.63% \par             10-Year/11 am   5.91%                 5.86% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Rattaphol Onsanit and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2266 0744; djnews.bangkokdowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Hilary McCully and Ven Ram [ 11-08-06 1104GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1028 1861  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060811e28b000oy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
