\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Thai Baht Ends Up, Hits 6.5-Yr High; Short-End Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2006\par 13:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2006, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht extended its rally to end just off a six-and-a-half year high Friday as a torrent of offshore selling continued to weaken the dollar despite suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Thai long-term government bonds were mostly unchanged, but prices of short-term treasury bills rose due to expectations that interest rates have peaked. The pressure from the short end caused prices of some medium-term bonds to rise as well.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at THB37.36, down from THB37.46 at the Asian close Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Offshore players continued to dump the dollar, which has been on a losing streak against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently due to expectations that U.S. interest rates may have peaked.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar slid to THB37.28 in the afternoon, its lowest level since January 2000. It reached an intraday high of THB37.44 in the morning.  \par \par \uc2 But the U.S. unit staged a good recovery in late trade due to buying that was likely a combination of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action and players' adjustments to the dollar's rebound against key Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the Japanese yen.  \par \par \uc2 Traders suspect Bank of Thailand once again bought dollars to help limit the baht's strength. Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula confirmed late Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been active in the market. Traders said the greenback could sink to THB37.15 in foreign markets over the long weekend with the local market closed Monday for a public holiday, unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 'If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps in during the holiday, support (for the dollar-baht exchange rate) would be around THB37.23-THB37.30,' said a local trader. 'If not, it could fall to THB37.15 by Tuesday morning.'  \par \par \uc2 Thai Finance Minister Thanong Bidaya attempted to assist the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  with some mild verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday by saying the baht's strength during the past 2-3 days is likely a short term situation, and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the means to temper the effects of volatile capital flows.  \par \par \uc2 'There is no unusual movement in the market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also monitoring the market closely,' Thanong told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 -0-   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020060811e28b005sg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
