\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Ctrl Bk Chief:US Deficits May Cause Rapid Cap Flows  \b0\par\par\uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2006\par 05:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--A widening of U.S. deficits could spur a new round of rapid massive capital movements, but the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Wednesday that it is prepared for such an eventuality.  \par \par \uc2 Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula declined to say if the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  had in mind an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets or something more than that. [ 09-08-06 0356GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 "We have our measures ready should there be any sudden drop in the value of the dollar," Pridiyathorn said.  \par \par \uc2 In the first four months of this year, funds flowed out of U.S. assets into other regions, including Asia, on concerns over a slowing U.S. economy. But soon after, substantial capital returned to the U.S. markets on investors' increased aversion to assets in emerging markets. This cycle has been repeated in the past few months, he said.  \par \par \uc2 On the baht, Pridiyathorn said that while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  intends to manage the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep it at a level that would help exporters, it won't resist the baht's market trend.  \par \par \uc2 He also said that exporters should brace themselves for a firmer baht and shouldn't 'fancy' that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will ease to around THB40 against the dollar anytime soon.Around 0510 GMT, the dollar was at THB37.65, down slightly from THB37.70 in late trading Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Thailand's economic fundamentals remain strong, and private investment should resume oncea new government is in place, he said.  \par \par \uc2 He reiterated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forecast that the Thai economy will grow by 4.0%-5.0% this year and by 4.0%-5.25% next year.  \par \par \uc2 "Although the projected growth rates are not that high, they are considered satisfactory under the current situation," he said.  \par \par \uc2 But he allayed fears that the economy might face a new round of crisis, given the level of the country's foreign reserves - around $60 billion - and a strong growth in exports.  \par \par \uc2 Thailand faced a massive economic crisis in 1997, brought on by a depletion of the country's foreign reserves after a failed defense of its fixed exchange-rate mechanism.  \par \par \uc2 -By Bangkok Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Ven Ram [ 09-08-06 0534GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060809e2890004u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
