\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends Higher On Broad Dlr Weakness; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 567 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2006\par 12:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended higher Wednesday on dollar selling by offshore players amid broad weakness in the U.S. unit versus Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped cap the baht's rise, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices closed slightly higher after an auction showed that demand remains firm relative to moderate supply.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at THB37.82, down from THB38.23 at Tuesday's close.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit hit its intraday high of THB38.02 in the morning, and was then dragged down by offshore selling.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said hedge funds squared long-dollar positions built up as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rising over the past two days, prompting other players to join the selling.  \par \par \uc2 Weaker-than-expected U.S. housing data was a key reason for the reversal Wednesday of the dollar's rebound this week against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The greenback fell to an intraday low of THB37.73 in late trade.  \par \par \uc2 "But it rebounded just before the market close, possibly on buying by the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a trader at a local bank said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar is expected to trade between THB37.70 and THB38.15 overnight. [ 17-05-06 1031GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Most Thai government bond yields ended slightly lower as Wednesday's auction showed that domestic demand remains firm and the baht's rebound raised the prospect of foreign demand returning, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from primary dealers Tuesday also continued to support market sentiment.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Thailand sold Wednesday THB3.4 billion of the government bond due May 2009 at an average 5.3539%, up from 5.3145% at last week's auction. The increase wasn't as much as feared however, and high bid coverage at 5.63 times confirmed that demand was very strong relative to supply.  \par \par \uc2 Another THB2.5 billion of the bond due March 2021 was sold at an average 5.8813%, down from 5.9135% at the previous offering of the issue on April 26.  \par \par \uc2 The average secondary market bid on the May 2009 issue was down two basis points at 5.330% and the July 2013 bid eased one basis point to 5.447%, while the July 2016 bid fell one basis point to 5.553% and the March 2021 bid dropped one and 1/2 basis points to end at 5.893%, according to the Web site of the Thai Bond Market Association.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said yields could resume rising if the baht starts to weaken again or U.S. consumer price inflation data due later Wednesday indicates that U.S. and local interest rates will rise further than expected. But otherwise the mild downward correction of the increases seen earlier this week is likely to continue.  \par \par \uc2 The most-active overnight money market interest rate was expected to have remained at 4.65%.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market     Term            Wednesday              Tuesday \par Interbank  Overnight/ \par            Most-Active     4.65000% (Estimate)    4.65000% \par Repurchase Overnight/Close 4.62500%               4.59375% \par            14-Day/Close    4.75000%               4.75000% \par Bibor      3-Month/11 am   5.24750%               5.24125% \par            6-Month/11 am   5.40078%               5.39766% \par THB Fix    6-Month/11 am   5.47173%               5.47976% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Rattaphol Onsanit and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2266 0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Hilary Mc Cully [ 17-05-06 1051GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1028 1861  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060517e25h000ng\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
