\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends Flat,Off High On Oil Cos Buying;Bonds Flat  \b0\par\par\uc2 532 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2006\par 12:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended flat against the U.S. dollar in light trade Wednesday, with late buying mainly by oil companies wiping out early gains, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Thai government bond prices also ended flat in razor-thin trade as most investors were on the sidelines ahead of the long weekend. Thai markets will be closed Friday for a public holiday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at THB37.64, unchanged from Tuesday's close. The greenback opened softer at THB37.54 amid general dollar weakness against most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gradually eased to an intraday low of THB37.49 in the afternoon.  \par \par \uc2 "However, dollar buying in late trade erased (the baht's) early gains after the dollar rebounded against other regional units. Besides, market participants are also cautious about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to have stepped in several times to defend the THB37.50 level since last week," said a dealer at a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 Still, dealers said they don't detect any signs of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent sessions.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said Wednesday the baht is starting to stabilize and that the bank did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation.  \par \par \uc2 The governor said capital continues to flow into the country in a "seeping" manner.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market didn't react much to the uncertainty in Thai politics Wednesday, as its movement was directed largely by that of regional units.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai Administrative Court said Wednesday it won't be able to rule on the validity of the April 2 elections until May 15. This will prolong the political uncertainty and delay the formation of new government.  \par \par \uc2 "Politics is largely discounted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. I think the market won't react until a concrete decision comes out," said another trader at a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 Traders expect the dollar to be held in a THB37.50-THB37.70 range Thursday. [ 03-05-06 1035GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Thai government bond yields ended barely changed amid a holiday mood and lack of fresh factors, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 There was no bond auction Wednesday, and none will be held Thursday. The auction will resume next week.  \par \par \uc2 The average bid on the government bond due December 2008 was flat at 5.310%, while the July 2013 bid rose one basis point to 5.46%. The July 2016 bid and the March 2021 were both flat at 5.55% and 5.87% respectively, according to the Thai Bond Market Association's Web site.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight money market interest rate remained high as local banks kept high money reserves ahead of an upcoming long weekend.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market     Term            Wednesday              Tuesday \par Interbank  Overnight/ \par            Most-Active     4.66000% (Estimate)    4.66000% \par Repurchase Overnight/Close 4.59375%               4.59375% \par            14-Day/Close    4.75000%               4.75000% \par Bibor      3-Month/11 am   5.22188%               5.21828% \par            6-Month/11 am   5.37313%               5.37063% \par THB Fix    6-Month/11 am   5.49380%               5.50145% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Phisanu Phromchanya and Suttinee Yuvejwattana, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 226