\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends Up On Broad Dollar Weakness; Bonds Jump  \b0\par\par\uc2 713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 2006\par 13:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended higher against the dollar Friday in line with broad weakness in the U.S. unit but suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped limit the dollar losses, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the latest political developments and economic data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had little impact on the baht amid thin trade ahead of a long weekend.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices finished sharply higher on hefty buying interest spurred by the view that the domestic interest rate tightening cycle may soon end.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at THB37.50, down from THB37.59 at Thursday's close after it slid to a fresh six-year low of THB37.46 in the morning.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the dollar was tracking its decline against other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the morning.  \par \par \uc2 "However, the greenback rebounded later on suspected buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it dipped to THB37.46," a local trader said.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is rather quiet in a holiday mood despite the development on political fronts," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Thai markets will be closed Monday for the Labor Day holiday.  \par \par \uc2 The Administrative Court canceled a Saturday by-election to be held in 14 constituencies that remained undecided after inconclusive snap polls April 2.  \par \par \uc2 The ruling came hours after the country's top judges said they couldn't immediately rule on the validity of April 2 general elections, but vowed that a verdict would be delivered soon to steer the country out of a deepening political crisis.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in the afternoon that Thailand swung to a trade surplus of $187 million in March due to strong export growth. The trade surplus, though lower than economists' expectations, had been expected.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the dollar will move within a THB37.40-THB37.70 range in trading Tuesday. [ 28-04-06 1149GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Government yields dropped significantly on active buying by both offshore parties and local funds, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also believed to have bought short-term bonds, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Buying sprees were inspired by Finance Minister Thanong Bidaya's comment Thursday that current interest rate levels appeared to be sufficient to control inflation, they said.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said part of the capital inflows, which caused the recent baht rally, have been parked in bonds, driving bond demand further.  \par \par \uc2 "It's a herd behavior. It seems like the whole market is now on the buy side....I've also seen lots of buying orders from local units of foreign banks today," a local financial institution dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Yields were also weighed by suspected buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in short-term bonds, specifically in one- to three-year issues, during the morning session, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Thailand sold THB17 billion worth of treasury bills Friday at average yields which were slightly lower than those of its previous auction, due to a belief that the rising trend in interest rates is over or will soon end.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold THB6 billion of 28-day t-bills at an average accepted yield of 4.50667%, THB6 billion of 91-day t-bills at an average 4.67583%, and THB5 billion of 182-day t-bills at an average 4.86900%.  \par \par \uc2 The average bid on the government bond due August 2008 was down nine basis points at 5.242%, while the July 2013 bid plunged almost 10 basis points to 5.410%. The July 2016 bid tumbled 10 basis points to 5.506%, and the bid on the March 2021 issue dropped nine basis points to 5.824%, according to the Thai Bond Market Association's Web site.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight money market interest rate was up slightly at 4.67% due to month-end demand and preparation for Monday's holiday.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market     Term            Friday                Thursday \par Interbank  Overnight/ \par            Most-Active     4.67000% (Estimate)    4.63000% \par Repurchase Overnight/Close 4.62500%               4.65625% \par            14-Day/Close    4.75000%               4.75000% \par Bibor      3-Month/11 am   5.21094%               5.20469% \par            6-Month/11 am   5.35938%               5.35563% \par THB Fix    6-Month/11 am   5.50317%               5.58565% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Rattaphol Onsanit and Phisanu Phromchanya, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2266 0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Michael Kitchen [ 28-04-06 1150GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1028 1861  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060428e24s0017l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
