\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends Down;Oil Cos,Importers Buy Dlrs; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 527 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2006\par 13:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended slightly lower against the U.S. dollar Friday on dollar buying by oil companies and local importers, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The baht also eased on concerns over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise, they said.  \par \par \uc2 Government bonds ended higher, continuing their rebound after recent losses.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at THB37.81, up from THB37.75 at Thursday's close. The U.S. unit traded between THB37.77 and THB37.89 Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the dollar rose to its intraday high in the morning, tracking a broad dollar rebound before selling by exporters trimmed gains.  \par \par \uc2 Although BOT \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns are likely to continue supporting the dollar, exporters are ready to sell on any gains as most are not expecting a strong dollar recovery in the near term, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar was supported by demand from oil companies and importers. Trading volume was thin as many players stayed on the sidelines amid worries about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a trader at a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 BOT Deputy Governor Bandid Nijathaworn said Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is closely monitoring \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to ensure that the baht doesn't move excessively.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said they suspected that agents of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in favor of the U.S. dollar on several occasions recently, but the BOT doesn't comment directly on current market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The dollar hit a six-year low at THB37.66 in offshore trade during a local holiday Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Traders expect the dollar to remain in a range of THB37.70-THB37.90 over the weekend. [ 21-04-06 1108GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Government bond yields ended lower in a further downward correction following \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Demand in the long end of the curve outstrips moderate supply, and many investors think there may be only one more 25-basis point hike in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 14-day repurchase market target rate during the current tightening cycle.  \par \par \uc2 However, as the 14-day rate is now 4.75%, the downside for short and medium yields is likely to be limited.  \par \par \uc2 The average bid for the government bond due August 2008 eased four basis points to 5.410%, the December 2014 bid dropped five basis points to 5.662%, the July 2016 bid was down six basis points at 5.707% and the bid on the March 2021 issue fell six basis points to 6.061%, according to the Thai Bond Market Association's Web site.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight money market interest rate is expected to have remained around 4.63%.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market     Term            Friday                 Thursday \par Interbank  Overnight/ \par            Most-Active     4.63000% (Estimate)    4.63000% \par Repurchase Overnight/Close 4.62500%               4.62500% \par            14-Day/Close    4.75000%               4.75000% \par Bibor      3-Month/11 am   5.18047%               5.17422% \par            6-Month/11 am   5.34078%               5.33609% \par THB Fix    6-Month/11 am   5.58085%               5.56709% \pa