\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends Up, Off Wednesday's 6-Yr High; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 711 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 2006\par 13:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended firmer against the U.S. dollar Thursday compared with the previous Bangkok close, but it was off the fresh six-year high set in offshore trade during the closure of local markets Wednesday, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Robust March trade data issued Thursday supported baht sentiment, but the effect was limited because the figures were in line with expectations and players were worried about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the dollar, they said.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices ended higher due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped extend Tuesday's mild upward correction of sharp recent losses, which had been caused by rising interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at THB37.75, down from THB37.98 at Tuesday's close in Asia but up from a fresh six-year low of THB37.66 reached Wednesday, when Thai financial markets were closed for a public holiday.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit opened Thursday at THB37.78 and stayed in a tight range of THB37.71 to THB37.82.  \par \par \uc2 "The baht has rallied a long way now and many people are seeing only limited upside. Meanwhile, concerns that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could step in anytime if the baht should rise further discouraged any attempt to drive the baht up significantly," said a dealer at a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Of Thailand Deputy Governor Bandid Nijathaworn said Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is closely monitoring \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to ensure that the baht doesn't move excessively.  \par \par \uc2 "The point is that we don't want the baht to be too volatile," he told reporters.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said they suspected that agents of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in favor of the U.S. dollar on several occasions recently, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment directly on current market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Bandid said the baht's recent strength was in line with that of other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , resulting from broad dollar weakness and capital inflows into the region.  \par \par \uc2 Thailand posted a customs-basis trade surplus of $324.5 million in March, ending a string of deficits since December, due mainly to strong growth in exports of agricultural and automotive products, the Ministry of Commerce said Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Exports in March grew 15.9% on year to $11.10 billion, while imports rose 1.3% to $10.78 billion. The preliminary figures are based on data from the customs department. Official data is due April 28 from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , excluding goods in transit and including some goods which don't pass through customs.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expected the dollar to trade in a range of THB37.70-THB37.85 overnight. [ 20-04-06 1114GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Government bond yields ended lower after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying extended a downward correction that began Tuesday, when a weekly auction showed that demand continued to outstrip moderate supply, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy bonds maturing in 10-15 years, and the effect was exaggerated in light trading volume, they said.  \par \par \uc2 The downside for yields is likely to be limited, however, as many investors still expect one more 25-basis point increase in the current tightening cycle in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 14-day repurchase market target rate, which is currently 4.75%.  \par \par \uc2 The average bid for the government bond due August 2008 fell five basis points to 5.447%, while the December 2014 bid plunged 11 basis points to 5.711%, the July 2016 bid skidded 11 basis points to 5.763% and the bid on the March 2021 issue dropped seven basis points to end at 6.123%, according to the Thai Bond Market Association's Web site.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight money market interest rate was expected to have remained around 4.63%.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market     Term            Thursday               Tuesday \par Interbank  Overnight/ \par            Most-Active     4.63000% (Estimate)    4.63000% \par Repurchase Overnight/Close 4.62500%               4.62500% \par            14-Day/Close    4.75000%               4.75000% \par Bibor      3-Month/11 am   5.17422%               5.15922% \par            6-Month/11 am   5.33609%               5.31969% \par THB Fix    6-Month/11 am   5.56709%               5.60313% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Phisanu Phromchanya and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2266 0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Hilary Mc Cully [ 20-04-06 1125GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1028 1861  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060420e24k000nu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
