\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Central banks act to limit gains  \b0\par\par\uc2 801 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2006\par 05:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, April 18 (Reuters) - Several Asian central banks were suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday to hold down their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had risen initially because of a growing view that U.S. interest rate increases could be near an end.  \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won <KRW=> rose as high as 951.8 per dollar and then retreated on worries about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Data on Tuesday showing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves had increased in the first half of April underpinned those concerns.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=> was quoted briefly at a six-year high of 37.85 per dollar but its gains were pared after some dealers spoke of possible dollar buying by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday and Tuesday. Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities last week also made traders wary.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar extended recent gains to 1.5999 per U.S. dollar <SGD=>, its strongest level in nearly eight years, before pulling back after dollar purchases by local banks, which dealers suspected were on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS).  \par \par \uc2 "To a degree the price move reflects broader dollar trends, but market participants also appear to be testing out how low they can take U.S. dollar/Sing dollar before the MAS reacts aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -wise," Lim Su Sian, an economist at the Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi, said in a note.  \par \par \uc2 However, Lim said the MAS seemed to be merely providing some defence for the U.S. dollar at the 1.6000 level rather than aggressively attempting to reverse the market's direction.  \par \par \uc2 Last Tuesday, the MAS stuck to a policy of gradual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation, surprising markets who were looking for it to allow a bigger rise in the trade-weighted Singapore dollar. The MAS conducts monetary policy by steering the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed band based on a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts said the Sing dollar's rise since the decision suggested the current policy permitted it to have a wider band and a steeper appreciation than most believed.  \par \par \uc2 DOLLAR TREND  \par \par \uc2 Apart from the won, which retained some of its gains, most of the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were either down or barely changed on the day, even though the U.S. dollar stayed soft against the yen <JPY=> and euro <EUR=>.  \par \par \uc2 Some of the early gains had come from expectations of an end to U.S. rate rises. Analysts said minutes from the Fed's March meeting and U.S. March housing data due later on Tuesday would be watched for further clues on rates.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said there was still some interest in buying the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of Chinese President Hu Jintao's visit to Washington this week, when he will come under pressure to allow the yuan to appreciate more rapidly.  \par \par \uc2 "It keeps bubbling in the background and is acting as a cap on dollar/Asia, but expectations are relatively low that there will be a huge announcement from Hu," said Westpac senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Sean Callow.  \par \par \uc2 But Hu was unlikely to say anything that would dash all expectations of yuan appreciation, particularly while in the United States, where he would be facing heavy pressure to do something to tackle global trade imbalances, Callow said.  \par \par \uc2 "So the risks of being short dollar/Asia are relatively low." \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0801 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       118.05         118.26       +0.18\par  Sing dlr        1.6028         1.6038       +0.06\par  Taiwan dlr      32.480         32.456       -0.07\par  Korean won      953.70         955.70       +0.21\par  Baht             37.96          37.92       -0.09\par  Peso             51.48          51.34       -0.27\par  Rupiah         8975.00        8985.00       +0.11\par  Rupee            45.21          45.10       -0.24\par  Ringgit         3.6715         3.6690       -0.07\par  Yuan            8.0198         8.0174       -0.03\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       118.05         117.96       -0.08\par  Sing dlr        1.6028         1.6625       +3.72\par  Taiwan dlr      32.480         32.850       +1.14\par  Korean won      953.70        1011.60       +6.07\par  Baht             37.96          41.11       +8.31\par  Peso             51.48          53.09       +3.13\par  Rupiah         8975.00        9835.00       +9.58\par  Rupee            45.21          45.04       -0.38\par  Ringgit         3.6715         3.7790       +2.93\par  Yuan            8.0198         8.0702       +0.63 ((Reporting\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 by Vidya Ranganathan, editing by Alan Raybould; Reuters Messaging: vidya.ranganathan.reuters.com@reuters.net; +65-68703090)) For the new Reuters scrolling global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  service please cli