\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends Down On Dollar Short Covering; Bonds Flat  \b0\par\par\uc2 638 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2006\par 12:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended softer against the U.S. dollar Wednesday on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hefty dollar buying by oil companies and dollar short covering by interbank players in a bid to limit exposures ahead of a long holiday weekend in Thailand, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Government bonds ended virtually flat in thin trade amid the holiday lull, as the country's financial markets will be closed Thursday and Friday for the traditional New Year's break.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at THB38.13, up from THB38.03 at Tuesday's close in Asia. The U.S. unit opened lower at THB37.96, following its losses earlier against the Singapore dollar.  \par \par \uc2 It fell to an intraday low of THB37.95, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is suspected to have stepped in to curb the baht's strength. The dollar shot to an intraday high of THB38.18 before selling by exporters capped gains.  \par \par \uc2 "Oil companies actively sought dollars to settle their business obligations. As the dollar rebounded, many interbank players also bought dollars to cover short in order to square out or trim their positions ahead of the upcoming long holidays," said a dealer at a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 Despite suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Assistant Governor Atchana Waiquamdee said Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  couldn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  much in the market to help stop the baht strengthening.  \par \par \uc2 "We can't set the market. We have to let the baht move in line with the market mechanism," Atchana said.  \par \par \uc2 She said the baht's strength was due to continued capital inflows and improved sentiment resulting from easing political concerns.  \par \par \uc2 "Don't look at baht strength as a key negative factor for exports. The main issue for exporters is their productivity. Actually, a strong baht helps the country a lot in terms of a lower value for oil imports," she said.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said Wednesday that recent capital inflows, the key driver of strength in the Thai baht, were to buy stocks rather than for speculation.  \par \par \uc2 "The current baht level is slightly stronger than other (regional) \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  thanks to huge capital inflows earlier in the year. But we think it will stabilize after this," Pridiyathorn said.  \par \par \uc2 Pridiyathorn said the current baht level is still competitive for exports, considering the recent strong export figures.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in the market since last Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Traders expect the dollar to find support at THB37.90, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is believed to take action, while firm resistance is pegged at THB38.30. [ 12-04-06 1020GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Government bond yields ended almost flat, as many players were away ahead of the holiday.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the Bank of Thailand tapped into the sleepy market, buying some long-term bonds with 10-year to 17-year maturities. Though the move helped limit rises in yields, it hardly stirred follow-through buying.  \par \par \uc2 The average bid for government bonds due December 2014 was up one basis point at 5.779%, while bids on the March 2012 issue rose one basis point to 5.656%, and bids on the March 2021 issue were flat at 6.136%, according to Thai Bond Market Association's Web site.  \par \par \uc2 The money market was also rather quiet ahead of the holiday, with interest rates mostly flat.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market     Term            Wednesday                Tuesday \par Interbank  Overnight/ \par            Most-Active     4.63000% (Estimate)    4.63000% \par Repurchase Overnight/Close 4.62500%               4.62500% \par            14-Day/Close    4.75000%               4.75000% \par Bibor      3-Month/11 am   5.13750%               5.11100% \par            6-Month/11 am   5.29938%               5.28225% \par THB Fix    6-Month/11 am   5.61013%               5.58891% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Phisanu Phromchanya and Rattaphol Onsanit, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2266 0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Graham Norris [ 12-04-06 1024GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1028 1861  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060412e24c000i8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
