\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Thai Baht Ends Off High On Possible  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ;Bonds Dn  \b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2006\par 13:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2006, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht was higher against the dollar late Tuesday on gains in some regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and equity-related inflows, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 However, the baht's rise was apparently capped by continued dollar buying by the Bank of Thailand, traders suspected.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices were quoted lower in line with the rising interest rate trend, but trading was razor-thin as most players were on the sidelines ahead of a long holiday for Thailand's traditional new year.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at THB38.03, down from THB38.14 at Monday's close in Asia. The U.S. unit spiraled down to a fresh six-year low of THB37.92 before noon. The intraday low was the lowest since April 2000, beating Monday's record of THB37.98.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit clung around its intraday high of THB38.05 in the morning, then continued its retreat.  \par \par \uc2 'The dollar's slide was more in line with its losses against the yuan and the Singapore dollar than the dollar-yen, while the (equity) inflows remained supportive to the baht,' said a local trader.  \par \par \uc2 Soon after it dived to the intraday low, the dollar bounced back.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have stepped in around THB37.95, although its authorities avoided mentioning any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when asked by reporters.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Bandid Nijathaworn said that the Thai baht's current strength was mainly due to steady capital inflows.  \par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't determined whether those inflows are for investment or for speculation, Bandid told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 'We will monitor the market closely to make sure that the baht is not too strong,' he said, but added that his remarks weren't meant to suggest the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market at the moment.  \par \par \uc2 Bandid's remark followed comments by Bank of Thailand Governor Pridayathorn Devakula, who said earlier Tuesday that the baht exchange rate moved in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Traders expect that the dollar's support at THB37.95 should hold Wednesday morning, with resistance at THB38.10.  \par \par \uc2 -0-   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020060411e24b008ho\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
