\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Ctrl Bk Chief:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  To Cap Baht Rise Monday  \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 12:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Monday to limit the strength of the baht, Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said late Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "We stepped in to manage (the baht) slightly Monday, but we didn't do anything today, just let it moves in line with the market," Pridiyathorn told reporters. [ 21-03-06 1107GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The dollar weakened sharply Monday to end at THB38.625, down from THB39.02 at Friday's close in Asia and THB38.84 early Monday, catching up with last week's fall in the dollar-yen pair. Pridiyathorn didn't elaborate on the extent of Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which would have curbed the losses in the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended higher Tuesday, reaching THB38.83 at the Asian close, boosted by importers' demand for the U.S. unit and tracking the dollar's rebound against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's assistant governor, Atchana Waiquamdee, told reporters Tuesday that the dollar weakened Monday due to recent poor U.S. economic data, which has sparked concerns that the Federal Reserve will soon end its tightening cycle.  \par \par \uc2 "But the dollar recovered today, making the baht weaker, after Bernanke's comment this morning," Atchana said.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke said the current flatness of the U.S. Treasury yield curve doesn't signal an impending slowdown in the U.S. economy.  \par \par \uc2 Market players viewed Bernanke's speech as slightly hawkish despite the absence of an outlook for monetary policy, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Bernanke's speech "was noncommittal, which meant overall he made the case for the market to stay where it is," said Claudio Piron, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JPMorgan.  \par \par \uc2 -By Bangkok Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Hilary Mc Cully [ 21-03-06 1155GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060321e23l000hn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
