\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends Dn, Ctrl Bk Sales Suspected; Long Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 855 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2006\par 12:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended weaker against the U.S. dollar in Asian spot trade Wednesday on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dollar supportive comments by Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Long-term government bond prices closed slightly higher, as the results of the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee meeting overnight supported the view that global interest rates will peak in the first half of the year. The U.S. federal funds target rate rose 25 basis points to 4.5% as expected, but the statement issued after the meeting appeared to indicate that there mightn't be a need to raise rates much further.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar ended at THB39.23, up from THB39.00 at Tuesday's Asian close.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar opened lower at THB38.905 on selling by offshore players.  \par \par \uc2 However, buying by local importers and oil companies limited the losses and pushed the U.S. unit higher, said dealers, who suspected that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  agents were also behind the corrective rise in the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "Short-covering was triggered after the dollar/baht breach above the 39.00 figure. The pair was boosted further in the afternoon by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comment," said a dealer at a major local bank.  \par \par \uc2 Pridiyathorn said Wednesday afternoon that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is watching to make sure that the baht's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate doesn't affect exports, but it won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as much as some exporters would like.  \par \par \uc2 "The baht's strength isn't affecting exports because we are taking care of it," Pridiyathorn said.  \par \par \uc2 There was no confirmation of Wednesday's suspected dollar buying, because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on daily market actions.  \par \par \uc2 The governor indicated, however, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  mightn't be able to satisfy exporters who want to see the baht around THB40 to the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will try to manage the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's float as much as it can, but too much management would cause problems, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Pridiyathorn said flows from New York into Asian markets were the reason for the baht's strength since the beginning of the year, as Thai stock prices were at attractive levels relative to earnings per share.  \par \par \uc2 Equity-linked inflows were very strong earlier this year, before easing significantly lately, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Political concerns over the controversy surrounding the sale of a stake last month in Shin Corp. by Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra's family to Singapore's Temasek Holdings are also weighing on baht sentiment, dealers said. Although the premiere's family will escape any taxation on the THB73.3 billion ($1.88 billion) deal, the Securities & Exchange Commission is investigating his adult son's reporting of share transfers in the years prior to the deal.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar to find next resistance at THB39.30 and immediate support at THB39.00. [ 01-02-06 1155GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Thai long-term government bond yields declined slightly due to a lack of supply this week and on the view that global and local interest rates will peak in the first half of the year, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 There was no government bond auction Wednesday, but regular weekly offerings resume Feb. 8.  \par \par \uc2 The FOMC meeting results helped support the view that interest rates will peak soon, but short and medium-term yields were flat or little changed due to lingering uncertainty about where the U.S. fed funds rate and the local 14-day repurchase rate will peak between 4.5% and around 5%.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to raise its 14-day repurchase market target rate by 25 basis points to 4.5% at its next policy meeting on March 8.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai Bond Market Association said the average bid yield on the government bond due August 2008 was up less than half a basis point at 4.943%. The March 2012 bid was down nearly two basis points to 5.257%. The July 2013 bid was down almost two basis points to 5.324%. The July 2016 bid dropped three basis points to 5.509%, and the August 2019 bid fell two-and-a-half basis points to end at 5.689%.  \par \par \uc2 Also Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold at auction THB1 billion worth of six-year government-guaranteed Bangkok Mass Transit Authority bonds at an accepted yield of 5.345%. The yield was in line with expectations about 10 basis points above the government bond yield curve.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai overnight interbank most-active rate was expected to have remained unchanged at 4.14%.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market     Term            Wednesday              Tuesday \par Interbank  Overnight/ \par            Most-Active     4.14000% (Estimated)   4.14000% \par Repurchase Overnight/Close 4.09375%               4.12500% \par            14-Day/Close    4.25000%               4.25000% \par Bibor      3-Month/11 am   4.60000%               4.59922% \par            6-Month/11 am   4.80000%               4.80000% \par THB Fix    6-Month/11 am   4.97675%               4.95452% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Phisanu Phromchanya and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2266 0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Hilary Mc Cully [ 01-02-06 1202GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1028 1861  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060201e221000l8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
