\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Thai  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  says no baht  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 195 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2006\par 06:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Jan 19 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 interven\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the baht's sharp gains during early trade on Thursday, Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said.  \par \par \uc2 He said the baht strength was due partly to inflows related to an impending major transaction in shares in Shin Corp , the company founded by Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra and the focus of intense rumours for several weeks.  \par \par \uc2 "We have not done anything. Its gain has been due to an inflow of funds for a Shin share deal. After the inflow, the baht moved normally in line with market forces," Pridiyathorn said.  \par \par \uc2 "Capital inflows are good and I have nothing against them." he added.  \par \par \uc2 Pridiyathorn said he had no information on whether there would be any additional inflows of funds for a Shin share deal.  \par \par \uc2 The baht rose to a 9-\u189\'00\'BD month high against the dollar earlier on Thursday, when \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders in Bangkok said they expected the BOT to interevene later, although they had not seen anything at that stage.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-THAILAND-BAHT (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060119e21j000a5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
