\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Ctrl Bk Not  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  As Baht Weakens -Governor  \b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2006\par 06:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said Tuesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to make the Thai baht weaken.  \par \par \uc2 "We don't do anything in the current baht weakness. There is nothing wrong in the market. We have no need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Pridiyathorn said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0525 GMT, the dollar was at THB39.75, down from THB39.81 earlier Tuesday, but still above THB39.69 at Monday's close in Asia. [ 17-01-06 0529GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the market last week to curb the baht's sharp strength. The baht has risen around 3% so far this year, in line with the dollar's broad weakness and heavy equity-related inflows.  \par \par \uc2 "We have no concerns now," Pridiyathorn said.  \par \par \uc2 The capital inflow is "normal", but it has started to level off since late last week, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Foreigners still were net buyers of THB1.87 billion worth of Thai stocks Monday, but the amount of buying was lower significantly from a high of over THB15 billion seen in a single day earlier this month.  \par \par \uc2 -By Bangkok Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Ven Ram [ 17-01-06 0600GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060117e21h0004j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
