\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Ctrl Bk Has  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  Against Baht -Dep Governor  \b0\par\par\uc2 392 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 2006\par 10:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Bandid Nijathaworn said Monday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets recently to limit the rise of the baht.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to prevent any excessive movement in the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said.  \par \par \uc2 "We will closely monitor the baht and we will make sure that it doesn't fluctuate too much," Bandid told a news conference after the close of markets. [ 09-01-06 0959GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Bandid said the baht has been rising since the start of the new year due to the strength of the yen and to heavy capital inflows possibly related to portfolio adjustment by foreign investors.  \par \par \uc2 The baht's strength also tends to attract inflows, so the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be monitoring markets for any increase in volatile short term flows, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Thailand will also have to continue monitoring markets to determine whether the baht's strength has affected the country's export competitiveness, but its rise hasn't exceeded those of other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said.  \par \par \uc2 Bandid said the baht had risen only 0.73% against the U.S. dollar since Friday, while the Japanese yen was up 1.77%, the Korean won 1.16%, the Indonesian rupiah 1.06% and the Singapore dollar 0.75%.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was quoted at the end of the Asian trading day Monday at THB39.77, off a seven-month low of THB39.72 on buying by suspected agents of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell from THB40.05 at Friday's close and THB40.35 Thursday, after opening the year at THB41.025.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar has fallen sharply against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since U.S. data released Friday showed nonfarm payrolls up by 108,000 jobs last month, versus expectations of a rise of 215,000.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, capital inflows have been supported by heavy net buying by foreign investors of THB38 billion worth of local shares on the Stock Exchange of Thailand last week.  \par \par \uc2 The SET Index rose 2% Monday to close at 762.29 points with trading volume boosted by continued foreign inflows, local analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 -By the Bangkok Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; 662 266 0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Hilary Mc Cully [ 09-01-06 1045GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060109e219000j5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
