\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Ctrl Bk Hasn't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkt- Governor  \b0\par\par\uc2 242 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2006\par 11:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said late Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent the Thai baht from rising.  \par \par \uc2 "We let the baht move in line with the market mechanism. If we are in the market (to manage the baht), it (the baht) won't be this strong," Pridiyathorn told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht ended in Asian spot trade Thursday at THB40.35 against the U.S. dollar, a fresh seven-month high, due mainly to equity-related inflows and broad dollar weakness. [ 05-01-06 1038GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Asked about the lower-than-expected consumer price index reading in December, Pridiyathorn said it was in line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's expectations.  \par \par \uc2 "We expect that the inflation in the near term will be around 6%. In the first quarter, inflation will likely be slightly over 6%, possibly in a range of 5.8%-6.2%," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The Ministry of Commerce announced Wednesday that the headline inflation rate was 5.8% on year in December, down 0.1% from the previous month, as lower food prices helped offset rising oil prices.  \par \par \uc2 Economists surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires had on average expected the CPI to rise 6.0% on year and 0.1% on month.  \par \par \uc2 -By Bangkok Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com [ 05-01-06 1115GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060105e215000d