\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends Dn On Corporate Dlr Buying; Long Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2005\par 11:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended lower in Asian spot trade Friday in moderate volume due to dollar buying by local companies after the U.S. unit plunged to a fresh one-month low Thursday, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  around THB40.90 kept the dollar well bid, they said.  \par \par \uc2 Long-term government bond prices continued to rise only slightly, as a rally this week sparked by the relatively dovish tone in U.S. and Thai policy statements appeared to have run its course.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at THB40.96, up from Thursday's close of THB40.92, after moving in a range of THB40.89-THB40.97.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened marginally lower at THB40.91, tracking its weakness against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 However, concern over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around THB40.90 and active buying by importers and local firms helped the dollar to rebound moderately.  \par \par \uc2 "The market isn't confident enough that the dollar's bearish momentum can continue much longer, especially when it is well aware that the (Thai) authority is there to fend off any excessive baht strength," said a dealer at a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit is expected to remain range bound between THB40.90 and THB41.05 over the weekend. [ 16-12-05 1043GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Thai long-term government bond yields closed only slightly lower Friday, after steep declines this week following the U.S. and local policy meetings, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 A dealer said an upward correction in yields might occur next week, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 14-day repurchase market target rate is still expected to rise another 50-75 basis points following a 25-basis point increase to 4% on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Yields of medium-term bonds and issues with terms up to six years were mostly flat or up slightly.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai Bond Market Association said the average secondary market bid on the government bond due November 2009 was almost unchanged at 5.304%, the March 2012 bid was up nearly one basis point at 5.576%, the December 2014 bid slid two basis points to 5.702%, and the December 2019 bid was down one basis point to end at 5.956%.  \par \par \uc2 The most-active overnight interbank rate was expected to remained unchanged at 3.90%, although lenders were quoting hopeful offers around 4.00%, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Quotes for money market interest rates with terms of six months or more eased in line with expectations that the 14-day target rate might peak sooner than expected, but the three-month Bangkok Interbank Offered Rate, or Bibor, continued to advance closer to 4.5%.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market     Term            Friday                 Thursday \par Interbank  Overnight/ \par            Most-Active     3.90000% (Estimate)    3.90000% \par Repurchase Overnight/Close 3.93750%               3.93750% \par            14-Day/Close    4.00000%               4.00000% \par Bibor      3-Month/11 am   4.45609%               4.44594% \par            6-Month/11 am   4.70844%               4.70969% \par THB Fix    6-Month/11 am   4.83300%               4.84060% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Tom Fox and Phisanu Phromchanya, Dow Jones Newswires; 662 266 0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Gauri Bhatia [ 16-12-05 1044GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1028 1861  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051216e1cg000h1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\pi