\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends Firmer On Broad Dlr Weakness; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 802 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2005\par 12:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended at a fresh one-month high in Asian spot trade Thursday in hefty volume due to the dollar's generally weak tone against most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 A more dovish tone in the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee's policy statement this week has been taken as a signal that U.S. interest rates will soon be peaking.  \par \par \uc2 The change in the global interest rate outlook has weakened the U.S. dollar on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. It also helped to trigger buying on the local bond market, where prices of government bonds rose sharply for the second consecutive day.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at THB40.92, down from THB41.05 Wednesday, but off an intraday low of 40.90.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened easier at THB40.98, tracking losses against the yen and other Asian units.  \par \par \uc2 Its fall was accelerated by stop-loss selling after its drop to below THB41.00 overnight, but buying by local corporations and suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped to limit its losses.  \par \par \uc2 "Selling orders were from both onshore and offshore players this morning, some to (stop losses) and some to build up short (dollar) positions amid a steady drop in the dollar against the yen," a trader at a local bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Equities-related inflows also supported the baht. Foreign investors were net buyers of a combined THB4.73 billion of Thai stocks Tuesday and Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "However, there is talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to limit the dollar's fall around THB40.90. Active buying by local corporate also helped the dollar to regain some ground in late trade," the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit is expected to find firm support at THB40.85, with resistance at THB41.10.  \par \par \uc2 Sentiment toward the baht was also bolstered by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move Wednesday to raise its 14-day repurchase market target rate by 25 basis points to 4% and its promise of further policy tightening until real interest rates are positive, or above the level of inflation.  \par \par \uc2 The tone of the Bank of Thailand's policy statement was also slightly more dovish than previous ones. It raised the 14-day rate by only 25 basis points versus 50 basis points at each of the previous two meetings, citing a moderation in inflation as well as in private consumption and investment.  \par \par \uc2 In response, JPMorgan cut its forecast for the 14-day target rate by 25 basis points to a likely peak of 4.75% by the second quarter of 2006. [ 15-12-05 1109GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Thai government bond yields closed sharply lower Thursday, as the end of uncertainty over U.S. and local policy meetings this week released pent-up demand, and on expectations that global and local interest rates could peak sooner than expected, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The current round of buying will rebuild thin trading portfolios and reverse some losses before the year-end closing of account books, a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 But selling might follow in the first few weeks of the new year, as interest rates are expected to rise again in the first quarter of 2006.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai Bond Market Association said the average secondary market bid on the government bond due November 2009 fell 13 basis points to 5.300%, the March 2012 bid dropped 13 basis points to 5.570%, the December 2014 bid slid 10 basis points to 5.722%, and the December 2019 bid was down 11 basis points at 5.963%.  \par \par \uc2 The most active overnight interbank rate was expected to drop to 3.90% as liquidity returned to normal after a sharp rise to 4.10% Wednesday when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate hike played havoc with money market flows, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight repurchase market rate has already settled at 3.93750%, versus 3.68750% prior to the interest rate increase, indicating that the most active overnight interbank rate will likely settle in a range of 3.90%-3.95%.  \par \par \uc2 Quotes for money market interest rates with terms of six months or more eased in line with expectations that the 14-day target rate might peak sooner than expected, but the three-month Bangkok Interbank Offered Rate, or Bibor, continued to advance closer to 4.5%.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market     Term            Thursday               Wednesday \par Interbank  Overnight/ \par            Most-Active     3.90000% (Estimate)    4.10000% \par Repurchase Overnight/Close 3.93750%               3.93750% \par            14-Day/Close    4.00000%               4.00000% \par Bibor      3-Month/11 am   4.44594%               4.44172% \par            6-Month/11 am   4.70969%               4.71984% \par THB Fix    6-Month/11 am   4.84060%               4.90428% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Tom Fox and Phisanu Phromchanya, Dow Jones Newswires; 662 266 0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Genevieve Soledad [ 15-12-05 1123GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1028 1861  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051215e1cf000kg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
