\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends Flat In Lackluster Trade; Long Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 658 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2005\par 12:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht finished flat against the dollar in Asian spot trade Friday on lack of clarity over the U.S. unit's direction against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and no fresh domestic leads, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Long-term government bond prices resumed an upward correction of sharp losses over the past several weeks, after easing Thursday, on demand from big funds attracted by higher yields.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at THB41.14, unchanged from Thursday's close. The U.S. unit moved in a tight range of THB41.12 to THB41.18 Friday.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is rather quiet today without any fresh leads. Many interbank players are now squaring their positions pending any clear trend for the dollar in the short-term," said a dealer at a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the dollar also stayed rangebound on fears that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has appeared to step in on either side of the market when the exchange rate moves substantially.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers allayed fears that the uncertainty over the pending EGAT PCL IPO, Likely Thailand's largest-ever IPO, will have no impact on the baht.  \par \par \uc2 The Supreme Administrative Court will decide Tuesday whether or not to halt the IPO. Even if the court decides to stop the IPO, there shouldn't be any immediate effect on capital outflows as no substantial funds have been brought in directly for participation in the IPO. Foreign funds have adjusted existing portfolios in the local market to make room for the EGAT shares, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the dollar should remain in a tight range overnight between buy orders from local oil companies around THB41.10 and sell orders from exporters anywhere above THB41.20. [ 11-11-05 1107GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Long-term government bond yields resumed a downward correction of the sharp increases seen in recent weeks due to demand from large funds, but medium-term yields added to yesterday's mild reversal, rising under pressure from the interest rate trend, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The downward correction can continue in the long run as long as the big funds are still buying, but yields are likely to remain under upward pressure in the next few months as interest rates will likely still be rising.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai Bond Dealing Center said the average bid on the government bond due November 2009 edged up one basis point to 5.900%, but the March 2012 bid fell three basis points to 6.248%, the December 2014 bid was down two basis points to 6.380%, and the December 2019 bid edged down one basis point to end at 6.868%.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Thailand said Friday the coupon rate for five-year government savings bonds to be offered to retail investors Nov. 15-24 was set at 6.25%, versus 5.25% for five-year savings bonds issued in mid-September. The coupon was set slightly higher than the five-year yield of 6.11%, extrapolated from the yield curve for regular government bonds issued to institutional investors, in line with coupon rates for previous savings bond issues.  \par \par \uc2 The most active overnight interbank rate was likely to remain at 3.68%, dealers said. The rate might come under some slight upward pressure in the middle of next week as monthly corporate tax payments are due on Nov. 16.  \par \par \uc2 Quotes for most term interest rates were higher in line with the broad trend.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market     Term            Friday                 Thursday \par Interbank  Overnight/ \par            Most-Active     3.68000% (Estimate)    3.68000% \par Repurchase Overnight/Close 3.68750%               3.68750% \par            14-Day/Close    3.75000%               3.75000% \par Bibor      3-Month/11 am   4.30278%               4.30139% \par            6-Month/11 am   4.65250%               4.65069% \par THB Fix    6-Month/11 am   4.78778%               4.80618% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Phisanu Phromchanya and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 662 266 0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Gauri Bhatia [ 11-11-05 1107GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1028 1861  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051111e1bb000nr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
