\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Thai Baht Ends Flat In Lackluster Trade; Long Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2005\par 12:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht finished flat against the dollar in Asian spot trade Friday on lack of clarity over the U.S. unit's direction against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and no fresh domestic leads, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Long-term government bond prices resumed an upward correction of sharp losses over the past several weeks, after easing Thursday, on demand from big funds attracted by higher yields.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at THB41.14, unchanged from Thursday's close. The U.S. unit moved in a tight range of THB41.12 to THB41.18 Friday.  \par \par \uc2 'The market is rather quiet today without any fresh leads. Many interbank players are now squaring their positions pending any clear trend for the dollar in the short-term,' said a dealer at a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the dollar also stayed rangebound on fears that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has appeared to step in on either side of the market when the exchange rate moves substantially.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers allayed fears that the uncertainty over the pending EGAT PCL IPO, Likely Thailand's largest-ever IPO, will have no impact on the baht.  \par \par \uc2 The Supreme Administrative Court will decide Tuesday whether or not to halt the IPO. Even if the court decides to stop the IPO, there shouldn't be any immediate effect on capital outflows as no substantial funds have been brought in directly for participation in the IPO. Foreign funds have adjusted existing portfolios in the local market to make room for the EGAT shares, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the dollar should remain in a tight range overnight between buy orders from local oil companies around THB41.10 and sell orders from exporters anywhere above THB41.20.  \par \par \uc2 -0-   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020051111e1bb007k9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
