\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah breaks 10,000 mark, Taiwan dlr weak  \b0\par\par\uc2 791 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2005\par 06:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Sept 14 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah strengthened past the psychologically important 10,000-per-dollar mark on Wednesday on the back of improving investor confidence after monetary tightening in the past two weeks.  \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar hovered close to its lowest level in at least eight years against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of export rival South Korea <TWDKRW=R> on expectation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will prevent gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a widely expected rate rise on Thursday aimed at stamping out inflation expectations.  \par \par \uc2 Other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were little changed as a smaller-than-expected U.S. trade deficit for July supported the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah <IDR=> gained almost 1 percent from late Asian trading on Tuesday and was quoted at a three-week high of 9,980 per dollar in early Asian trades.  \par \par \uc2 It gave up some of those gains by the afternoon and was bid at 10,025 per dollar at 0822 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained more than 17 percent since hitting a four-year low of 11,750 on Aug. 30 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to calm financial markets by raising its key rate by 125 basis points and requiring banks to park a greater share of deposits as reserve with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a bid to tighten money supply.  \par \par \uc2 "Foreign investors who sold the rupiah last month are trying to collect it now," said a Jakarta \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer.  \par \par \uc2 "It's all about the supporting news," he said referring to the rate rises and a government pledge to raise fuel prices early next month as part of a plan to cut its ballooning fuel subsidies.  \par \par \uc2 Ratings agency Fitch said on Tuesday it expected further aggressive monetary tightening in Indonesia in coming weeks.  \par \par \uc2 TAIWAN DOLLAR  \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> weakened to 32.811 per dollar, trading close to last week's 10-month lows after a top \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official warned on Tuesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was too strong compared with regional peers and did not reflect the country's deteriorating trade performance.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already weakened 3.5 percent in the third quarter against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 IDEAglobal said the verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor was seen by the local market as an attempt to ward off strength in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the event of a 25 basis point rise in the benchmark interest rate on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll of 13 analysts showed seven expected a 12.5 basis points rise in the key discount rate while the others forecast a 25 basis point rise.  \par \par \uc2 IDEAglobal said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warnings tilted the balance of expectations to a 25 basis points rise.  \par \par \uc2 "We, however, would also view the statements as testimony to the authorities' competitiveness concerns and as such would continue to expect the Taiwan dollar upside to lag its regional counterparts into early fourth quarter," IDEAglobal said in a note.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht traded on Wednesday close to Tuesday's three-month high against the Singapore dollar <SGDTHB=R> in the wake of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's higher-than-expected 50 basis points rate increase last week -- the seventh rate rise since last August.  \par \par \uc2 IDEAglobal said the trend could reverse as Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the baht's gains in check to support local exporters.  \par \par \uc2 Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose more than $500 million in the week ended Sept. 2 indicating \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0801 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       110.48         110.46       -0.02\par  Sing dlr        1.6789         1.6787       -0.01\par  Taiwan dlr      32.770         32.741       -0.09\par  Korean won     1025.30        1025.70       +0.04\par  Baht             40.95          40.90       -0.12\par  Peso             55.91          55.93       +0.04\par  Rupiah        10010.00       10070.00       +0.60\par  Rupee            43.91          43.89       -0.06\par  Ringgit         3.7688         3.7690       +0.01\par  Yuan            8.0912         8.0940       +0.03 Change on\par year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       110.48         102.45       -7.27\par  Sing dlr        1.6789         1.6310       -2.85\par  Taiwan dlr      32.770         31.920       -2.59\par  Korean won     1025.30        1035.10       +0.96\par  Baht             40.95          38.88       -5.05\par  Peso             55.91          56.28       +0.66\par  Rupiah        10010.00        9290.00       -7.19\par  Rupee            43.91          43.47       -1.00\par  Ringgit         3.7688         3.8000       +0.83\par  Yuan            