\par\par \b \uc2 Thai baht at 2-month peak, chart outlook bullish  \b0\par\par\uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2005\par 04:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 11 (Reuters) - The Thai baht extended this week's gains to hit its strongest level in almost two months against the dollar on Thursday and analysts said the outlook was bullish after a break of key chart barriers.  \par \par \uc2 Equity market gains, a rally in the yen and Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength following last month's revaluation of the yuan have helped the baht rebound about three percent from more than two-year lows hit in July.  \par \par \uc2 The baht <THB=> firmed a third of a percent from late Asian trading levels on Wednesday to 40.86 per dollar, its strongest showing since mid-June.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the baht's gains accelerated after breaking trendline resistance on Wednesday at 41.40 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The baht is now flirting with chart resistance at 40.80, a support level for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that was broken in June.  \par \par \uc2 "As long as dollar/baht trades below 41.31, the target is for a move to 40.44," said Winston Tang, technical analyst at 4CAST in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 A move to 40.44 per dollar would take the baht to where it traded in early June. This level provided support during the decline against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Tang said momentum indicators showed some signs of the baht being overbought but added these were not strong yet.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the rebound in the baht, it remains this year's worst performing Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said further gains in the yen, which the baht tracks closely, could push the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 40.80 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has rallied amid optimism about growth after weathering political upheaval this week over plans for a snap election following the government's defeat in a parliamentary vote on postal privatisation.  \par \par \uc2 "Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are taking a bit more of a cue from the yen, which has recovered after the postal vote defeat," said Thio Chin Loo, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at BNP Paribas. "The technical picture is bullish for the baht."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the stronger baht and will leave the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move in line with market forces, a senior bank official said late on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -BAHT|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|Z|IF|PHD|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050811e18b0004r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
