\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  regimes  \b0\par\par\uc2 1,246 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2005\par 13:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, July 22 (Reuters) - Asia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimes grabbed the spotlight after China revalued the yuan against the U.S. dollar and said it would manage it against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a move which sent regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher.  \par \par \uc2 Malaysia was quick to follow China's shift on Thursday evening, scrapping its seven-year-old peg and adopting a managed float. That leaves Hong Kong as the last major economy in Asia with a peg against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 In general, Asian economies explicitly or implicitly shadow the U.S. dollar. But the regimes vary greatly -- the Singapore dollar is floated against basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  while South Korea has an independently floating won.  \par \par \uc2 The following summary, drawn from official sources and investment bank reports, is based on the International Monetary Fund's definitions for fixed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pegs, managed floats with varying degrees of fluctuations, and independent floats.  \par \par \uc2 FIXED PEG  \par \par \uc2 --------------  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG DOLLAR <HKD=>  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong adjusted its linked exchange rate system in May for the first time since 1998, moving its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a band between 7.75 and 7.85 to the U.S. dollar from a asymmetric peg that set a floor of 7.8 per U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The initial peg was part of a \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Board Arrangement created on October 17, 1983, in response to a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. Under the board's rules, the Hong Kong dollar monetary base has to be matched by equivalent foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 MANAGED FLOATS:  \par \par \uc2 -------------------  \par \par \uc2 CHINESE YUAN OR RENMINBI <CNY=>  \par \par \uc2 After essentially pegging the yuan near 8.28 per dollar since the Asian crisis, China on Thursday revalued it to 8.11 and tied it to an undisclosed basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of trading partners.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan will be allowed to move 0.3 percent above or below the previous day's close against the U.S. dollar, and by 1.5 percent against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Theoretically, the trading band allows the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to edge higher, but China has had such flexibility since 1994 but has not used it since 1996, instead holding the yuan almost still.  \par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily, buying and selling yuan to maintain the new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band.  \par \par \uc2 Prior to the Thursday's move, the yuan was kept in a 0.04 percent band centred on a rate of around 8.278 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 China had followed a dual exchange rate since 1979 but unified those rates in 1994 to create a crawling yuan peg.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan appreciated from 8.7 per dollar to around 8.3 between 1994 and 1996, and continued to fluctuate around there until the Asian crisis, when Beijing rejected advice to devalue like its neighbours and virtually fixed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  instead.  \par \par \uc2 MALAYSIAN RINGGIT <MYR=>  \par \par \uc2 Malaysia on Thursday dropped its seven-year-old peg of 3.8 to the U.S. dollar in favour of a managed float against an undisclosed basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , moving soon after China did.  \par \par \uc2 Malaysia has said the aim of its exchange rate policy is to maintain stability with \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of major trading partners. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  used to float until a flight of capital and a collapse in its value during the 1997/98 Asian financial crisis prompted authorities to impose capital controls and fix the ringgit.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR <SGD=>  \par \par \uc2 Since 1981, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore conducts monetary policy by steering the Singapore dollar in an undisclosed band against an undisclosed trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rather than setting an interest rate as many central banks do.  \par \par \uc2 Economists say the regime is a combination of the band, basket and crawl \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  systems.  \par \par \uc2 The MAS runs policy by letting the nominal effective exchange rate (NEER) appreciate or depreciate, either by shifting the mid-point of the band or adjusting its width. Economists say the U.S. dollar and dollar-bloc \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  make up the biggest proportion of the trade-weighted basket.  \par \par \uc2 Policy shifted from neutral to a tightening bias in April 2004 via a gradual appreciation of the mid-point of the NEER.  \par \par \uc2 The Sing dollar is freely convertible on the trade account and has very minimal restrictions on capital flows.  \par \par \uc2 INDIAN RUPEE <INR=>  \par \par \uc2 Economists say the Reserve Bank of India uses a monitoring band for the rupee, which allows it to float within a band determined by the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of India's top five trading partners, adjusted for inflation levels.  \par \par \uc2 Markets believe the width of the band is five percent on either side of this neutral real effective exchange rate (REER), and the RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the band is breached.  \par \par \uc2 The RBI regularly publishes data on the REER base period and neutral value, but with a lag.  \par \par \uc2 The current unified exchange rate was adopted in 1993 after a balance of payments crisis led to devaluations in 1991.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee is not fully convertible on the capital account. There are still some limits on residents borrowing overseas, on residents converting local assets into foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and on the access foreigners have to Indian debt markets.  \par \par \uc2 THAI BAHT <THB=>  \par \par \uc2 Massive capital outflows forced Thailand to abandon the baht's peg against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on July 2, 1997, triggering a big devaluation against the dollar that marked the onset of the Asian financial crisis.  \par \par \uc2 Thailand adopted a managed float. Like other Asian central banks operating under similar regimes, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  is averse to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  often in the market.  \par \par \uc2 Selective capital controls exist. There are strict limits on baht positions held by foreigners and offshore trading in baht is negligible.  \par \par \uc2 INDONESIAN RUPIAH <IDR=>  \par \par \uc2 Indonesia switched to a freely floating rupiah from a managed float in August 1997 during the Asian crisis. Several exchange controls remain.  \par \par \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to help the rupiah, which fell more than five percent against the dollar in the first half of 2005. To stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also banned sales of rupiah securities by non-residents.  \par \par \uc2 INDEPENDENTLY FLOATING:  \par \par \uc2 ------------------------  \par \par \uc2 KOREAN WON <KRW=> <KRW=KFTC>  \par \par \uc2 The won was floated in December 1997 and is one of Asia's most actively traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea runs an inflation-targeting policy, but the government dictates \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and keeps a watchful eye on the won's competitiveness. This occasionally leads to strains between the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the finance ministry.  \par \par \uc2 Foreigners have greater access to South Korean capital markets than to most others in emerging Asia, yet there are some restrictions on offshore won trading and on local banks' positions in won.  \par \par \uc2 The won non-deliverable forward (NDF) market that has developed as a consequence is among the most liquid in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 The yen-won is a popular cross rate, traded in the belief that Seoul likes to keep the won competitive versus the yen because of the overlap between South Korean and Japanese exports.  \par \par \uc2 PHILIPPINE PESO <PHP=>  \par \par \uc2 The peso is allowed to trade in a wider band than most other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is prone to volatile swings in response to political developments. It is also sensitive to data on the Philippines' large fiscal deficit and on remittances from overseas Filipinos, a major source of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with limited official reserves, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  occasionally. It also adjusts reserve requirements, and the rate at which they are remunerated, to help smooth the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-ASIA-FACTBOX-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|SI|SNS|SNI|PHD|IF|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050722e17m000yh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
