\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Fin Min: Strong Yuan, Weaker Oil To Cut Deficits  \b0\par\par\uc2 612 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2005\par 10:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Thai Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak said Friday that the revaluation of the Chinese yuan will help to cut the country's trade and current account deficits.  \par \par \uc2 "The baht has strengthened less than the yuan, so it will benefit Thai exports," Somkid told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 And with global crude oil prices declining at the same time, "the trade and current account deficits are likely to be less than forecast," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said recently that he expected the current account to swing to a deficit around $2.5 billion, or less than 2% of gross domestic product this year, from a surplus of $7.29 billion last year.  \par \par \uc2 Somkid said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be monitoring the baht closely to ensure that its movements aren't too volatile when local players return to the market Monday morning after a long weekend. Thai markets and financial institutions are closed Friday for a public holiday.  \par \par \uc2 However, any volatility resulting from the yuan revaluation will only be short term, he said.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula told reporters separately Friday that there has been no excessive volatility so far, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has prepared measures to reduce volatility if necessary. He didn't elaborate.  \par \par \uc2 Commerce Minister Thanong Bidiya said separately Friday that it will take about two months to gauge the effects of the yuan revaluation, but that as long as the baht doesn't strengthen below THB40 to the dollar the country's exports won't be hurt.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was quoted in offshore trading Friday at THB41.345, down from THB41.79 prior to the decision by the People's Bank of China to drop the yuan's de facto peg to the dollar in favor of a managed float against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In the process, the yuan was initially revalued about 2% to CNY8.1100 to a dollar from CNY8.2765.  \par \par \uc2 Pridiyathorn said late Thursday he was pleased with the change in China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime because it will help to stabilize regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and facilitate trade, which will be good for everyone.  \par \par \uc2 And now that the uncertainty surrounding the yuan has eased, "the baht should be less volatile," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The baht and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been fluctuating in recent months as investors speculated about the timing of China's move, appreciating in anticipation of a yuan revaluation when they thought the time was near, and depreciating when it failed to arrive.  \par \par \uc2 Usara Wilaipich, an economist in Bangkok for Standard Chartered Bank, said late Thursday that the yuan regime change will probably mean the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other regional central banks may not need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as much to protect the competitiveness of their countries' exports.  \par \par \uc2 Usara said Thai exports should benefit from lower export prices in dollar terms if the baht appreciates less than the yuan and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but over the long term, the benefits for Thailand and other regional suppliers of China's massive export industry are less clear.  \par \par \uc2 If the Chinese economy or its export growth slows as a result of the yuan's appreciation, the fall in income for its suppliers could be a greater factor for them than the price advantage provided by more competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates.  \par \par \uc2 "Exports from (Thailand and) the region to China could slow down, and in that case, the income effect is larger than the price effect," Usara said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Tom Fox and Suttinee Yuvejwattana, Dow Jones Newswires; 662 266 0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Mary de Wet [ 22-07-05 0851GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050722e17m000e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
