\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends Dn, Off 9-Mo Low; Short Bonds Dn Sharply  \b0\par\par\uc2 719 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2005\par 13:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended weaker after hitting a nine-month low against the U.S. dollar in Asian spot trade Tuesday, tracking the losses of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a surging dollar, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices drifted lower ahead of the start of a new series of weekly auctions on Wednesday, while prices of short-term \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds fell sharply ahead of an increase in short-term interest rates expected later in the month.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar finished at THB41.55, up from THB41.43 at the Asian close Monday, and just off a nine-month high of THB41.57.  \par \par \uc2 Expectations that the U.S. will continue raising interest rates for now, especially if U.S. payrolls data come out as strongly as expected Friday, supported the dollar against most global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Payrolls are expected to show a rise of 200,000 in June, much more than the 75,000 increase reported in May.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was also helped higher against the Japanese yen, a regional trendsetter, as Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi won only a thin five-vote majority in a key vote on postal system reform. The vote cast doubts on his government's ability to push through further reforms.  \par \par \uc2 There was little fresh local news moving the baht, but sentiment has been hurt by a string of current-account deficits in the three months to May.  \par \par \uc2 One trader said it was unlikely that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday, as the baht's move wasn't so great and it was in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Traders expected the dollar to trade in a range of THB41.45 to THB41.60 overnight, subject to any further volatility in the dollar-yen exchange rate. [ 05-07-05 1104GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Thai long-term government bond yields drifted higher Tuesday under pressure from a rising interest-rate trend, but most investors were sidelined ahead of the start of a new series of weekly auctions on Wednesday, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The auction will give indications of real levels of demand from funds and insurance companies, which are expected to be more than adequate to absorb supply in the long end of about THB4.5 billion per week.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai Bond Dealing Center said the average bid on the government bond due November 2009 bid was up 2 basis points at 3.463%. The March 2012 bid jumped almost 3 basis points to 3.859%. The December 2014 bid rose one-and-a-half basis points to 3.981%, and the August 2019 bid added one-and-a-half basis points to finish at 4.349%.  \par \par \uc2 Expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 14-day repurchase market target rate could rise by 25 basis points to 2.75% as early as the next monetary policy meeting on July 20 pushed short-term yields sharply higher.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Thailand auctioned Tuesday THB5 billion of its 28-day bonds at an average 2.315%, up from 2.055% at last week's auction. Another THB5 billion of 63-day \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds was sold at an average 2.436%, up from 2.260%, and THB15 billion of 364-day bonds at an average 2.936%, up from 2.856%.  \par \par \uc2 The most-active overnight interbank rate likely fell to 2.48% or 2.49% Tuesday, from 2.50% the previous day, as liquidity tied up for accounting purposes at the end of the first half of the year flowed back into the system, dealers said. The overnight repurchase market rate ended flat, having eased back on Monday to 2.46875% from 2.50% over the half-year end.  \par \par \uc2 Quotes for term interest rates were also mostly higher under pressure from the expected interest rate trend.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market     Term            Tuesday                Monday \par Interbank  Overnight/ \par            Most-Active     2.48%-2.49% (Estimate) 2.50000% \par Repurchase Overnight/Close 2.46875% (Actual)      2.46875% \par            14-Day/Close    2.50000%               2.50000% \par Bibor      3-Month/11 am   2.76792%               2.75333% \par            6-Month/11 am   2.90139%               2.90139% \par THB Fix    6-Month/11 am   3.25331%               3.23139% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 662 266 0744; tom.fox@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Paul Baylis [ 05-07-05 1119GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1028 1861  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050705e175000id\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
