\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends Dn On Late Dlr Rally; Bonds Dn On Supply  \b0\par\par\uc2 862 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2005\par 13:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht hit a fresh six-month low against the dollar in Asian spot trade Wednesday as onshore firms rushed to buy the U.S. unit when as it made a late charge against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Sentiment toward the baht was hurt by a report from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  that, based on customs department data, Thailand recorded a trade deficit of $1.55 billion in the month of April.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices rose in continuing gains after the finance ministry said Tuesday afternoon that it was canceling auctions scheduled from June 1 to July 6, and reducing the amount to be sold on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar finished at THB40.16, up from THB40.04 at the Asian close Tuesday, just off a six-month high of THB40.17.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit opened down and slid to an intraday low of THB39.96 tracking its early weakness against the Japanese yen, a regional trendsetter, amid renewed talk of a possible revaluation of the Chinese yuan.  \par \par \uc2 The Financial Times reported overnight that the U.S. had asked China through unofficial envoys to revalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 10%. But China reportedly said it would not be influenced by external pressure.  \par \par \uc2 Sentiment toward the baht soured after the customs department said exports were 13% on year in April to $8.24 billion, but imports were up 30% on year to $9.79 billion due to surging imports of oil and steel. Exports were interrupted by several holidays during the month.  \par \par \uc2 Deputy Prime Minister Somkid Jatusripitak, who also serves as finance minister, said the deficit was not a concern as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds substantial \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves on hands.  \par \par \uc2 The baht wasn't affected immediately, because the dollar was still testing intraday lows against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 But after players failed to take the U.S. unit into new lows for the second time Wednesday afternoon, they chased the dollar back up against the yen and most other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sparking a buying spree in late trade against the baht.  \par \par \uc2 Local oil firms and importers bought dollars aggressively, and exporters removed their sell orders.  \par \par \uc2 Some dealers said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cool the dollar's momentum at the Asian close.  \par \par \uc2 Technical charts suggest that after breaking strong resistance at THB40, the dollar could head toward THB40.265, and then THB40.41 in the coming weeks. Support is likely overnight at THB40.00, with major support at THB39.80. [ 25-05-05 1134GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Thai government bond yields ended sharply lower Wednesday in continuing losses after news the previous afternoon that June auctions had been canceled, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Profit taking by funds took yields off lows, however, along with uncertainty over what levels of supply might be upcoming to help finance planned infrastructure projects.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expected yields to level off around current levels pending further supply news.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai Bond Dealing Center said the two-year \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond traded Wednesday around 3.13%, down from 3.16% the previous day. The average bid on the government bond due December 2006 was virtually unchanged at 3.002%. The November 2009 bid fell 4 basis points to 3.523%. The March 2012 bid plunged 6 basis point to 3.900%. The December 2014 bid eased 3 basis points to 4.122%, and the December 2019 bid lost 2 basis points to end at 4.537%.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Thailand auctioned Wednesday THB1.5 billion of seven-year bonds due March 2012 at an average yield of 3.876%, down from 4.055% at last week's auction.  \par \par \uc2 An official from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the remaining auctions in the schedule were canceled because the government budget will be balanced this year, and the Treasury's refinancing needs were reduced after receiving a share of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's net profit for 2004. No figures were provided. A new supply schedule is likely to be announced in the first half of June, the official said.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight interbank rate was quoted late Wednesday around 2.25%, unchanged from the most-active level of the previous day. The overnight repurchase market rate also ended flat at 2.25%.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said overnight rates will remain firm due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowing. The Bank of Thailand supplemented its daily heavy borrowing in the regular afternoon repurchase market with light additional borrowing Wednesday in the morning bilateral repurchase market.  \par \par \uc2 Most quotes for term interest rates were unchanged because an interest-rate increase of 25 basis points likely in June or July has largely been priced in by related markets.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market     Term            Wednesday              Tuesday \par Interbank  Overnight/ \par            Most-Active     2.25000% (Estimate)    2.25000% \par Repurchase Overnight/Close 2.25000% (Actual)      2.25000% \par            14-Day/Close    2.25000%               2.25000% \par Bibor      3-Month/11 am   2.64922%               2.64922% \par            6-Month/11 am   2.85000%               2.85000% \par THB Fix    6-Month/11 am   3.01646%               3.03087% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Tom Fox and Maytinee Wasumadee, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2266 0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Paul Baylis [ 25-05-05 1140GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1028 1861  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050525e15p000mg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
