\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Thai Baht Ends Dn On Late Dlr Rally; Bonds Dn On Supply  \b0\par\par\uc2 428 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2005\par 14:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht hit a fresh six-month low against the dollar in Asian spot trade Wednesday as onshore firms rushed to buy the U.S. unit when as it made a late charge against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Sentiment toward the baht was hurt by a report from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  that, based on customs department data, Thailand recorded a trade deficit of $1.55 billion in the month of April.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices rose in continuing gains after the finance ministry said Tuesday afternoon that it was canceling auctions scheduled from June 1 to July 6, and reducing the amount to be sold on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar finished at THB40.16, up from THB40.04 at the Asian close Tuesday, just off a six-month high of THB40.17.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit opened down and slid to an intraday low of THB39.96 tracking its early weakness against the Japanese yen, a regional trendsetter, amid renewed talk of a possible revaluation of the Chinese yuan.  \par \par \uc2 The Financial Times reported overnight that the U.S. had asked China through unofficial envoys to revalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 10%. But China reportedly said it would not be influenced by external pressure.  \par \par \uc2 Sentiment toward the baht soured after the customs department said exports were 13% on year in April to $8.24 billion, but imports were up 30% on year to $9.79 billion due to surging imports of oil and steel. Exports were interrupted by several holidays during the month.  \par \par \uc2 Deputy Prime Minister Somkid Jatusripitak, who also serves as finance minister, said the deficit was not a concern as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds substantial \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves on hands.  \par \par \uc2 The baht wasn't affected immediately, because the dollar was still testing intraday lows against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 But after players failed to take the U.S. unit into new lows for the second time Wednesday afternoon, they chased the dollar back up against the yen and most other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sparking a buying spree in late trade against the baht.  \par \par \uc2 Local oil firms and importers bought dollars aggressively, and exporters removed their sell orders.  \par \par \uc2 Some dealers said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cool the dollar's momentum at the Asian close.  \par \par \uc2 Technical charts suggest that after breaking strong resistance at THB40, the dollar could head toward THB40.265, and then THB40.41 in the coming weeks. Support is likely overnight at THB40.00, with major support at THB39.80.  \par \par \uc2 -0-  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050525e15p0089c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
