\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends Down On Weak Yen, Local Stocks; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 777 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 13:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht fell against the U.S. dollar for an eighth consecutive day in Asian spot trade Wednesday, closing just off a 15-week low on weakness in the Japanese yen, equity-linked outflows and cross-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand from locally-based Japanese companies, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Medium- and long-term government bond prices ended higher after strong auction results boosted market sentiment.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar finished at THB39.35, up from THB39.265 at the Asian close Tuesday, after rising to a 15-week high of THB39.39 in early trade.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the U.S. unit's early gains were largely driven by its strength against the yen after Tokyo reported weaker-than-expected industrial production in February, with a 2.1% fall on month.  \par \par \uc2 Equity-related outflows also hurt the baht. Foreign investors sold a net THB1.48 billion worth of Thai shares Wednesday, after having sold a combined net THB7.0 billion in the six previous sessions.  \par \par \uc2 Thailand-based Japanese units continued to buy the yen outright in cross-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions through the U.S. dollar to make payments on loans and repatriate earnings before the end of Japan's fiscal year on March 31.  \par \par \uc2 "However, the dollar's rally cooled later in the day on exporter selling and suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Assistant Governor Nitaya Pibulratanagit said Wednesday that the baht was at an acceptable level, weakening against the dollar in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but she noted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when necessary.  \par \par \uc2 Trader said some interbank players also sold to take advantage of the dollar's sharp recent gains, booking profits ahead of the release of U.S. consumer data Thursday and nonfarm payrolls data Friday, both of which could influence the dollar's direction.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to retest resistance at THB39.40 overnight or Thursday, with the next resistance pegged at THB39.50. Support is expected at THB39.25. [ 30-03-05 1103GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Most Thai government bond yields fell after an auction demonstrated that demand driven by cash liquidity still outweighs moderate supply.  \par \par \uc2 The average accepted yield for a THB1.5 billion offering of the issue due March 2012 fell to 4.1559% from 4.2205% at last week's auction. Another THB1 billion of the issue due December 2019 was sold at an average 4.8252%, down from 4.8621% last week.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said Wednesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will consider both growth and inflation when determining interest rate policy, but that 2005 gross domestic product growth will exceed 5%.  \par \par \uc2 "It's possible that that key rate will rise by 1% (100 basis points) for the whole year as we still have six meetings left for this year," Pridiyathorn said.  \par \par \uc2 The governor's comments didn't affect the bond market, however, as they were in line with expectations. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 14-day repurchase market rate is currently 2.25%. Most economists expect an increase of 25 basis points when the policy committee next meets April 20, and further increases to around 3%-3.5% by year-end.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai Bond Dealing Center said the average bid late Wednesday on the government bond due November 2009 was down two basis points to 3.768%, the March 2012 bid dropped three basis points to 4.150%, the December 2014 bid fell six basis point to 4.524% and the December 2019 bid eased one basis point to 4.821%.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight interbank rate was quoted around 1.85%, lower in late trade as usual, but the most-active level likely remained around 1.90% due to earlier deals, dealers said. Liquidity was high as banks and clients had plenty of extra cash on hand for end-month wages and payments.  \par \par \uc2 Quotes for term interest rates were mostly down slightly, following steady increases in recent weeks, due to a lack of demand to borrow baht through the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap market, lowering implied yields of onshore swaps, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market     Term            Wednesday             Tuesday \par Interbank  Overnight/ \par            Most-Active     1.88%-1.9% (Estimate) 1.90000% \par Repurchase Overnight/Close 1.78125% (Actual)     1.78125% \par            14-Day/Close    2.25000%              2.25000% \par Bibor      3-Month/11 am   2.63641%              2.63891% \par            6-Month/11 am   2.83469%              2.83516% \par THB Fix    6-Month/11 am   3.01841%              3.04696% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Tom Fox and Maytinee Wasumadee, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Hilary Mc Cully [ 30-03-05 1128GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1028 1861  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050330e13u000js\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
